{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NmqqdRKYrvXtwB6viwyXTo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"15-Model Scaling Expansion\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"扩展至 15 模型（6 families），455 panels × 12 conditions 全量回归 + MI 矩阵 + 所有校正方法\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"status\": \"DONE (plan001_step1_full_v4)\",\n7\t      \"models\": 15,\n8\t      \"panels\": 455,\n9\t      \"conditions\": 12,\n10\t      \"eta_max_sig_ols\": \"11/12\",\n11\t      \"keff_sig_ols\": \"8/12 (7+/1-)\",\n12\t      \"eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"8/12\",\n13\t      \"keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/12\",\n14\t      \"eta_max_sig_bootstrap_v2\": \"5/12\",\n15\t      \"keff_sig_bootstrap_v2\": \"1/12\",\n16\t      \"eta_max_sig_mixed_effects\": \"7/12\",\n17\t      \"keff_sig_mixed_effects\": \"3/12\",\n18\t      \"dominance_ratio_bootstrap\": \"5:1\",\n19\t      \"gam_split\": \"6 targeted positive / 6 shared-bias negative\",\n20\t      \"min_eta_max_wins\": \"12/12\",\n21\t      \"confound_r\": 0.701,\n22\t      \"se_inflation_factor\": \"~2.5x\",\n23\t      \"rf_keff_sig\": \"2/2\",\n24\t      \"rf_r2_mmlu\": 0.734,\n25\t      \"rf_r2_arc\": 0.813\n26\t    },\n27\t    \"tables\": [\n28\t      {\n29\t        \"name\": \"Correction Method Comparison (Actual Results)\",\n30\t        \"columns\": [\n31\t          \"Method\",\n32\t          \"η_max sig\",\n33\t          \"K_eff sig\",\n34\t          \"K_eff dir\",\n35\t          \"Note\"\n36\t        ],\n37\t        \"rows\": [\n38\t          [\n39\t            \"OLS\",\n40\t            \"11/12\",\n41\t            \"8/12\",\n42\t            \"7+/1-\",\n43\t            \"Panel overlap inflated\"\n44\t          ],\n45\t          [\n46\t            \"Clustered SE (CR1, 15 clusters)\",\n47\t            \"8/12\",\n48\t            \"0/12\",\n49\t            \"-\",\n50\t            \"Conservative\"\n51\t          ],\n52\t          [\n53\t            \"Wild cluster bootstrap v2\",\n54\t            \"5/12\",\n55\t            \"1/12\",\n56\t            \"1+\",\n57\t            \"Max-p across 3 positions\"\n58\t          ],\n59\t          [\n60\t            \"Mixed effects\",\n61\t            \"7/12\",\n62\t            \"3/12\",\n63\t            \"3+\",\n64\t            \"Random judge intercepts\"\n65\t          ]\n66\t        ]\n67\t      }\n68\t    ],\n69\t    \"figures\": [],\n70\t    \"analysis\": \"已完成。η_max:K_eff 主导比从 OLS 的 1.4:1 升至 bootstrap 的 5:1，证明相对主导性在校正下 增强而非减弱。Benchmark 不对称（MMLU 4/6 vs ARC 1/6 存活 bootstrap）由 MMLU 4-choice 格式提供更多 scoring variance 解释。此结果构成 paper 的实证基础。\\n\\n已完成。15 模型覆盖 6 families × 3 capability tiers，提供 η_max 和 K_eff 充足方差。 SE 膨胀 ~2.5x 与 91/455 panel overlap 一致（claude-3-haiku 出现在 91 个 panels 中）。 η_max 存活校正因为它捕捉的是真实的个体 judge 脆弱性——不是 panel 重叠伪迹。 K_eff 崩溃因为其 OLS 显著性被 overlapping panels 的相关残差膨胀——clustered SE 控制共享 judge 成员关系后，K_eff 的独立信号太弱。GAM 6:6 分割源于攻击机制差异： targeted attacks 利用 judge 特异性弱点（diversity = 更多攻击面），shared-bias attacks 利用共性认知偏差（diversity = 部分 judges 免疫）。\"\n71\t  },\n72\t  {\n73\t    \"name\": \"Attack Surface Expansion\",\n74\t    \"description\": \"新增 3 种攻击类型（few-shot hijacking, persona manipulation, instruction override），在 15 模型 × 2 benchmarks 上运行，共 6 新 conditions\",\n75\t    \"results\": {\n76\t      \"new_attack_types\": 3,\n77\t      \"new_conditions\": 6,\n78\t      \"total_conditions\": 18,\n79\t      \"new_eta_max_sig_ols\": \"6/6\",\n80\t      \"new_keff_sig_ols\": \"4/6 (3+/1-)\",\n81\t      \"new_eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"5/6\",\n82\t      \"new_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/6\",\n83\t      \"new_eta_max_sig_bootstrap\": \"3/6\",\n84\t      \"new_keff_sig_bootstrap\": \"0/6\",\n85\t      \"combined_eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"13/18\",\n86\t      \"combined_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/18\",\n87\t      \"combined_dominance_ratio_clustered_se\": \"13:0\",\n88\t      \"gam_extended_split\": \"10 targeted positive / 8 shared-bias negative\",\n89\t      \"gam_new_attacks_classification\": {\n90\t        \"few_shot_hijacking\": \"targeted (positive K_eff)\",\n91\t        \"persona_manipulation\": \"shared-bias (negative K_eff)\",\n92\t        \"instruction_override\": \"targeted (positive K_eff)\"\n93\t      },\n94\t      \"new_r2_range\": [\n95\t        0.22,\n96\t        0.45\n97\t      ],\n98\t      \"min_eta_max_wins_extended\": \"18/18\"\n99\t    },\n100\t    \"tables\": [\n101\t      {\n102\t        \"name\": \"Extended Attack Taxonomy (Clustered SE)\",\n103\t        \"columns\": [\n104\t          \"Attack Type\",\n105\t          \"Mechanism\",\n106\t          \"Benchmark\",\n107\t          \"η_max sig?\",\n108\t          \"K_eff sig?\",\n109\t          \"K_eff GAM direction\"\n110\t        ],\n111\t        \"rows\": [\n112\t          [\n113\t            \"few-shot hijacking\",\n114\t            \"targeted\",\n115\t            \"MMLU\",\n116\t            \"Yes\",\n117\t            \"No\",\n118\t            \"positive\"\n119\t          ],\n120\t          [\n121\t            \"few-shot hijacking\",\n122\t            \"targeted\",\n123\t            \"ARC\",\n124\t            \"Yes\",\n125\t            \"No\",\n126\t            \"positive\"\n127\t          ],\n128\t          [\n129\t            \"persona manipulation\",\n130\t            \"shared-bias\",\n131\t            \"MMLU\",\n132\t            \"Yes\",\n133\t            \"No\",\n134\t            \"negative\"\n135\t          ],\n136\t          [\n137\t            \"persona manipulation\",\n138\t            \"shared-bias\",\n139\t            \"ARC\",\n140\t            \"Yes\",\n141\t            \"No\",\n142\t            \"negative\"\n143\t          ],\n144\t          [\n145\t            \"instruction override\",\n146\t            \"targeted\",\n147\t            \"MMLU\",\n148\t            \"Yes\",\n149\t            \"No\",\n150\t            \"positive\"\n151\t          ],\n152\t          [\n153\t            \"instruction override\",\n154\t            \"targeted\",\n155\t            \"ARC\",\n156\t            \"No\",\n157\t            \"No\",\n158\t            \"positive\"\n159\t          ]\n160\t        ]\n161\t      },\n162\t      {\n163\t        \"name\": \"Extended GAM Split Summary\",\n164\t        \"columns\": [\n165\t          \"Category\",\n166\t          \"Original (6 attacks)\",\n167\t          \"New (3 attacks)\",\n168\t          \"Total\",\n169\t          \"K_eff direction\"\n170\t        ],\n171\t        \"rows\": [\n172\t          [\n173\t            \"Targeted\",\n174\t            \"6/6 positive\",\n175\t            \"4/4 positive\",\n176\t            \"10/10\",\n177\t            \"positive (diversity harmful)\"\n178\t          ],\n179\t          [\n180\t            \"Shared-bias\",\n181\t            \"6/6 negative\",\n182\t            \"2/2 negative (persona×2)\",\n183\t            \"8/8\",\n184\t            \"negative (diversity protective)\"\n185\t          ]\n186\t        ]\n187\t      }\n188\t    ],\n189\t    \"figures\": [],\n190\t    \"analysis\": \"新攻击类型提供独立证据线，确认 η_max 主导性不依赖于特定攻击选择。GAM taxonomy 从 6:6 扩展至 10:8，mechanistic split 的稳健性增强——审稿人无法再质疑 taxonomy 是 cherry-picked 6 种 攻击的巧合。Instruction override 在 ARC 上 η_max 未显著（ARC 2-choice 格式对 instruction override 的 judge 间方差不敏感），与原始 benchmark asymmetry 一致。论文标题和核心叙事完全支持。\\n\\nFew-shot hijacking 利用模型在 in-context learning 上的个体差异——不同 judges 对 few-shot 示例的敏感度差异极大（GPT-4.1 vs Llama-8B 可差 3-5x），因此属于 targeted attack，η_max 捕捉最易受影响的 judge。Instruction override 利用 instruction-following 能力的模型间方差， 同样属于 targeted。Persona manipulation 利用 LLMs 对权威/身份线索的普遍敏感性——这是一种 共享认知偏差，不同能力模型都会受影响，因此属于 shared-bias，K_eff 方向为负（diversity 提供 部分免疫）。新攻击在 OLS 下延续 η_max 主导模式，但 K_eff 再次因 panel overlap 膨胀而 显著——clustered SE 后归零，与原 12 conditions 完全一致。GAM 扩展至 10:8 分割，clean taxonomy 覆盖 9 种攻击类型。\"\n191\t  },\n192\t  {\n193\t    \"name\": \"Random-Fault BFT Contrast Experiment\",\n194\t    \"description\": \"Monte Carlo 随机故障模拟作为 BFT 对照。每个 judge 以 η_j = 1 - clean_accuracy 独立失败，majority vote。对比 adaptive regime 证明 BFT 反转\",\n195\t    \"results\": {\n196\t      \"regime\": \"Random Fault (i.i.d.)\",\n197\t      \"conditions\": 2,\n198\t      \"monte_carlo_iterations\": 10000,\n199\t      \"rf_keff_sig_ols\": \"2/2\",\n200\t      \"rf_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"2/2\",\n201\t      \"rf_keff_sig_bootstrap\": \"2/2\",\n202\t      \"rf_keff_direction\": \"positive (2/2)\",\n203\t      \"rf_keff_std_beta_mmlu\": 0.215,\n204\t      \"rf_keff_std_beta_arc\": 0.379,\n205\t      \"rf_eta_sig_all_methods\": \"2/2\",\n206\t      \"rf_r2_mmlu\": 0.78,\n207\t      \"rf_r2_arc\": 0.81,\n208\t      \"adaptive_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/12\",\n209\t      \"adaptive_keff_sig_bootstrap\": \"1/12\",\n210\t      \"delta_r2_rf_vs_adaptive\": 0.48,\n211\t      \"go_nogo_gate\": \"PASS (RF K_eff ≥2/2)\"\n212\t    },\n213\t    \"tables\": [\n214\t      {\n215\t        \"name\": \"RF vs Adaptive Contrast (Key Metrics)\",\n216\t        \"columns\": [\n217\t          \"Metric\",\n218\t          \"Random Fault\",\n219\t          \"Adaptive\",\n220\t          \"Interpretation\"\n221\t        ],\n222\t        \"rows\": [\n223\t          [\n224\t            \"K_eff sig (OLS)\",\n225\t            \"2/2\",\n226\t            \"8/12 (7+/1-)\",\n227\t            \"Both appear significant under OLS\"\n228\t          ],\n229\t          [\n230\t            \"K_eff sig (Clustered SE)\",\n231\t            \"2/2\",\n232\t            \"0/12\",\n233\t            \"RF genuine; adaptive artifactual\"\n234\t          ],\n235\t          [\n236\t            \"K_eff sig (Bootstrap v2)\",\n237\t            \"2/2\",\n238\t            \"1/12\",\n239\t            \"Consistent contrast\"\n240\t          ],\n241\t          [\n242\t            \"K_eff std β (mean)\",\n243\t            \"+0.297\",\n244\t            \"+0.164\",\n245\t            \"RF effect larger and genuine\"\n246\t          ],\n247\t          [\n248\t            \"R²\",\n249\t            \"0.78-0.81\",\n250\t            \"0.25-0.35\",\n251\t            \"RF structurally determined; adaptive not\"\n252\t          ],\n253\t          [\n254\t            \"η_max sig (all methods)\",\n255\t            \"2/2\",\n256\t            \"5-8/12\",\n257\t            \"η_max genuine in both regimes\"\n258\t          ]\n259\t        ]\n260\t      },\n261\t      {\n262\t        \"name\": \"RF Per-Benchmark Detail\",\n263\t        \"columns\": [\n264\t          \"Benchmark\",\n265\t          \"η_max β\",\n266\t          \"K_eff β\",\n267\t          \"R²\",\n268\t          \"K_eff p (bootstrap)\"\n269\t        ],\n270\t        \"rows\": [\n271\t          [\n272\t            \"MMLU\",\n273\t            \"+0.482\",\n274\t            \"+0.215\",\n275\t            \"0.78\",\n276\t            \"0.003\"\n277\t          ],\n278\t          [\n279\t            \"ARC\",\n280\t            \"+0.551\",\n281\t            \"+0.379\",\n282\t            \"0.81\",\n283\t            \"<0.001\"\n284\t          ]\n285\t        ]\n286\t      }\n287\t    ],\n288\t    \"figures\": [],\n289\t    \"analysis\": \"这是论文的关键因果证据。RF 对照证明 K_eff 在满足 i.i.d. 假设时有真实效应——BFT 理论 在随机故障下成立。而 adaptive regime 下 K_eff 的 OLS 显著性完全是 panel overlap 的伪迹。 这不是\\\"diversity helps under RF but hurts under adaptive\\\"——K_eff 在两种 regime 下方向均 为正。区别是：RF 下 K_eff 的正关联是真实的（panel 结构决定了容错性），adaptive 下是膨胀的 （adversary 引入的策略方差使 panel 结构预测力崩溃）。此发现为 Contribution #2（BFT reversal evidence）提供了不可替代的因果论证。\\n\\n随机故障下 K_eff 显著的根本原因是 BFT 的 i.i.d. 假设成立：每个 judge 独立以固定概率犯错， panel 结构（多样性）直接影响冗余覆盖。K_eff 高的 panel 中 judges 的错误模式更不相关， majority vote 的容错能力与独立性成正比——这正是 BFT 的核心机制。K_eff 方向为正（diversity → higher error）因为高 K_eff panel 必然包含弱模型（r=0.70 tradeoff），而在 i.i.d. 体制下 弱模型的高错误率直接传导为 panel 错误率——但关键是 K_eff 的贡献是独立的、真实的（所有校正 方法均显著 2/2）。对照 adaptive regime：相同的 K_eff 在 OLS 下显著 8/12，但 clustered SE 后崩溃至 0/12——因为 adaptive adversary 引入了 panel 结构无法预测的策略方差，K_eff 的 apparent OLS 信号完全来自 panel overlap 膨胀。R² 差异（RF 0.78-0.81 vs adaptive ~0.30） 直接量化了 adaptive adversary 引入的不可预测性。GO/NO-GO gate 通过，BFT framing 得到 因果层面的支撑。\"\n290\t  },\n291\t  {\n292\t    \"name\": \"Capability-Matched Validation\",\n293\t    \"description\": \"在同一 capability tier 内（主要利用 9-model base tier, 84 panels）测试控制 η_max 方差后 K_eff 是否浮现为显著预测因子\",\n294\t    \"results\": {\n295\t      \"primary_tier\": \"base (9 models, 84 panels)\",\n296\t      \"within_tier_eta_max_variance_reduction\": \"65-70%\",\n297\t      \"within_tier_keff_eta_max_r\": 0.35,\n298\t      \"conditions\": 12,\n299\t      \"within_tier_keff_sig_ols\": \"5/12\",\n300\t      \"within_tier_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"2/12\",\n301\t      \"within_tier_keff_direction\": \"4+/1-\",\n302\t      \"within_tier_eta_max_sig_ols\": \"7/12\",\n303\t      \"within_tier_eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"4/12\",\n304\t      \"within_tier_dominance_ratio\": \"2:1\",\n305\t      \"within_tier_r2_mean\": 0.18,\n306\t      \"cross_tier_comparison\": {\n307\t        \"full_pool_dominance_ratio\": \"5:1\",\n308\t        \"within_tier_dominance_ratio\": \"2:1\",\n309\t        \"interpretation\": \"η_max still dominant but K_eff gains relative signal\"\n310\t      }\n311\t    },\n312\t    \"tables\": [\n313\t      {\n314\t        \"name\": \"Cross-Tier vs Within-Tier Comparison\",\n315\t        \"columns\": [\n316\t          \"Setting\",\n317\t          \"Panels\",\n318\t          \"K_eff-η_max r\",\n319\t          \"η_max sig (CL-SE)\",\n320\t          \"K_eff sig (CL-SE)\",\n321\t          \"Ratio\",\n322\t          \"R² mean\"\n323\t        ],\n324\t        \"rows\": [\n325\t          [\n326\t            \"Full pool (15 models)\",\n327\t            \"455\",\n328\t            \"0.70\",\n329\t            \"8/12\",\n330\t            \"0/12\",\n331\t            \"8:0\",\n332\t            \"0.30\"\n333\t          ],\n334\t          [\n335\t            \"Base tier (9 models)\",\n336\t            \"84\",\n337\t            \"0.35\",\n338\t            \"4/12\",\n339\t            \"2/12\",\n340\t            \"2:1\",\n341\t            \"0.18\"\n342\t          ],\n343\t          [\n344\t            \"Frontier tier (3 models)\",\n345\t            \"1\",\n346\t            \"-\",\n347\t            \"-\",\n348\t            \"-\",\n349\t            \"-\",\n350\t            \"-\"\n351\t          ]\n352\t        ]\n353\t      },\n354\t      {\n355\t        \"name\": \"Within-Tier K_eff Significant Conditions\",\n356\t        \"columns\": [\n357\t          \"Condition\",\n358\t          \"K_eff β\",\n359\t          \"K_eff p (CL-SE)\",\n360\t          \"Direction\",\n361\t          \"GAM confirms?\"\n362\t        ],\n363\t        \"rows\": [\n364\t          [\n365\t            \"mmlu×prompt_injection\",\n366\t            \"+0.31\",\n367\t            \"0.028\",\n368\t            \"positive\",\n369\t            \"Yes (targeted)\"\n370\t          ],\n371\t          [\n372\t            \"mmlu×score_manipulation\",\n373\t            \"+0.25\",\n374\t            \"0.041\",\n375\t            \"positive\",\n376\t            \"Yes (targeted)\"\n377\t          ]\n378\t        ]\n379\t      }\n380\t    ],\n381\t    \"figures\": [],\n382\t    \"analysis\": \"Capability-matched validation 提供了 disentangle η_max 和 K_eff 的准自然实验。关键发现： 即使在控制 η_max 方差后，K_eff 仍然是次要驱动因素（2:1 而非 1:1 或 K_eff 主导）。 论文可表述为：\\\"当 capability 差异被控制时，diversity 浮现为统计上可检测的次要因素——但在 自然 panel 组合中，capability 差异（通过 η_max）压倒性地主导脆弱性。\\\"这强化了 robustness-first 设计建议：先筛选 capability，再在筛选后的池中考虑 diversity。\\n\\n在同一 capability tier 内，η_max 方差降低约 65-70%（因为同 tier 模型能力接近），而 K_eff 方差保持（同 tier 模型仍来自不同 families/architectures）。η_max 和 K_eff 的 confound 从 r=0.70（全池）降至 r≈0.35（tier 内），解开了回归中的多重共线性。在此条件下，K_eff 的边际信号——通常被 η_max 的强效应淹没——变得可检测。OLS 下 5/12 显著；clustered SE 后 保留 2/12，表明 K_eff 有微弱但真实的独立效应。主导比从 5:1 降至 2:1，但 η_max 仍然 主导。这支持论文叙事：K_eff 有方向性关联但在全池分析中被 η_max 压倒——当人为控制 η_max 方差时 K_eff 才浮现，这恰恰说明在自然变异条件下 η_max 是主要驱动因素。此外，within-tier R² 均值仅 0.18，说明 tier 内的面板脆弱性预测力大幅下降——进一步证明 η_max 的跨 tier 方差是预测力的主要来源。\"\n383\t  },\n384\t  {\n385\t    \"name\": \"Two-Stage Panel Design Algorithm Benchmark\",\n386\t    \"description\": \"实现 robustness-first 两阶段算法（filter η > threshold → maximize K_eff），对标 5 个 baseline 策略\",\n387\t    \"results\": {\n388\t      \"baselines\": [\n389\t        \"random\",\n390\t        \"max_keff\",\n391\t        \"max_disagreement\",\n392\t        \"strongest_k\",\n393\t        \"uniform_family\"\n394\t      ],\n395\t      \"conditions\": 12,\n396\t      \"min_eta_max_wins\": \"12/12\",\n397\t      \"two_stage_vs_min_eta_max_improvement_pp\": [\n398\t        0.3,\n399\t        1.8\n400\t      ],\n401\t      \"two_stage_vs_min_eta_max_mean_improvement_pp\": 0.7,\n402\t      \"two_stage_wins_vs_min_eta_max\": \"7/12\",\n403\t      \"strategy_ranking\": {\n404\t        \"rank_1\": \"two-stage (robustness-first + K_eff)\",\n405\t        \"rank_2\": \"min_eta_max (robustness-first only)\",\n406\t        \"rank_3\": \"strongest_k\",\n407\t        \"rank_4\": \"uniform_family\",\n408\t        \"rank_5\": \"max_disagreement\",\n409\t        \"rank_6\": \"max_keff\",\n410\t        \"rank_7\": \"random\"\n411\t      },\n412\t      \"max_keff_vs_random\": \"worse in 8/12 (includes weak models)\",\n413\t      \"strongest_k_gap_from_min_eta_max\": \"1.2pp mean\",\n414\t      \"asr_advantage_range\": [\n415\t        0.038,\n416\t        0.511\n417\t      ]\n418\t    },\n419\t    \"tables\": [\n420\t      {\n421\t        \"name\": \"Strategy Comparison (Mean ASR across 12 conditions)\",\n422\t        \"columns\": [\n423\t          \"Strategy\",\n424\t          \"Mean ASR\",\n425\t          \"Rank\",\n426\t          \"Δ vs random (pp)\"\n427\t        ],\n428\t        \"rows\": [\n429\t          [\n430\t            \"two-stage\",\n431\t            \"0.112\",\n432\t            \"1\",\n433\t            \"-8.3\"\n434\t          ],\n435\t          [\n436\t            \"min_eta_max\",\n437\t            \"0.119\",\n438\t            \"2\",\n439\t            \"-7.6\"\n440\t          ],\n441\t          [\n442\t            \"strongest_k\",\n443\t            \"0.131\",\n444\t            \"3\",\n445\t            \"-6.4\"\n446\t          ],\n447\t          [\n448\t            \"uniform_family\",\n449\t            \"0.158\",\n450\t            \"4\",\n451\t            \"-3.7\"\n452\t          ],\n453\t          [\n454\t            \"max_disagreement\",\n455\t            \"0.172\",\n456\t            \"5\",\n457\t            \"-2.3\"\n458\t          ],\n459\t          [\n460\t            \"random\",\n461\t            \"0.195\",\n462\t            \"6\",\n463\t            \"0.0\"\n464\t          ],\n465\t          [\n466\t            \"max_keff\",\n467\t            \"0.208\",\n468\t            \"7\",\n469\t            \"+1.3\"\n470\t          ]\n471\t        ]\n472\t      },\n473\t      {\n474\t        \"name\": \"Two-Stage vs min_eta_max Per-Attack-Type\",\n475\t        \"columns\": [\n476\t          \"Attack category\",\n477\t          \"Conditions\",\n478\t          \"Two-stage better?\",\n479\t          \"Mean Δ (pp)\"\n480\t        ],\n481\t        \"rows\": [\n482\t          [\n483\t            \"Targeted\",\n484\t            \"6\",\n485\t            \"5/6\",\n486\t            \"-1.1\"\n487\t          ],\n488\t          [\n489\t            \"Shared-bias\",\n490\t            \"6\",\n491\t            \"2/6\",\n492\t            \"-0.3\"\n493\t          ]\n494\t        ]\n495\t      }\n496\t    ],\n497\t    \"figures\": [],\n498\t    \"analysis\": \"Two-stage 算法的边际改进（0.7pp）虽然在统计上一致但实际影响不大——论文应诚实呈现这一点。 核心 practical recommendation 保持不变：robustness-first screening 是关键步骤，K_eff 优化是可选的次要步骤。max_keff 策略的失败（差于 random）是论文叙事的有力支撑——直观的 \\\"多样化 panel\\\" 建议在实践中适得其反。\\n\\nmin_eta_max 策略赢 12/12 因为 η_max 是主导脆弱性驱动因素。两阶段策略在 min_eta_max 基础上提供边际改进（mean 0.7pp）：在已通过 robustness 筛选的 judge 子集中，K_eff 的微弱次要效应（在 capability-matched 设置中可检测，如 plan_004 所示）被利用。改进最大 的条件是 targeted attacks（K_eff 方向为正 = diversity 有害 → 在 robustness-screened 池中最小化 K_eff 有帮助）。改进最小的条件是 shared-bias attacks（K_eff 方向为负 → diversity 在这些条件下是保护性的 → 最大化 K_eff 更优）。max_keff 策略表现差于 random 因为最大化 diversity 必然引入弱模型（r=0.70 tradeoff），直接提高了 η_max。 strongest_k 与 min_eta_max 差距仅 1.2pp——因为最强模型通常也最鲁棒，但 min_eta_max 是直接优化目标函数而 strongest_k 是代理指标。\"\n499\t  },\n500\t  {\n501\t    \"name\": \"Per-Judge ASR Concentration Analysis\",\n502\t    \"description\": \"计算每个 panel × attack 的 per-judge ASR 分布的 Gini 系数和 Shannon 熵，量化 adaptive adversary 是否针对特定 judge\",\n503\t    \"results\": {\n504\t      \"panels\": 455,\n505\t      \"conditions\": 12,\n506\t      \"gini_targeted_mean\": 0.78,\n507\t      \"gini_targeted_range\": [\n508\t        0.72,\n509\t        0.85\n510\t      ],\n511\t      \"gini_shared_bias_mean\": 0.43,\n512\t      \"gini_shared_bias_range\": [\n513\t        0.35,\n514\t        0.52\n515\t      ],\n516\t      \"gini_targeted_vs_shared_mannwhitney_p\": \"<0.001\",\n517\t      \"entropy_targeted_mean\": 0.82,\n518\t      \"entropy_shared_bias_mean\": 1.45,\n519\t      \"gini_eta_max_correlation\": 0.83,\n520\t      \"top1_judge_asr_fraction_targeted\": 0.61,\n521\t      \"top1_judge_asr_fraction_shared\": 0.38\n522\t    },\n523\t    \"tables\": [\n524\t      {\n525\t        \"name\": \"ASR Concentration by Attack Category\",\n526\t        \"columns\": [\n527\t          \"Attack Type\",\n528\t          \"Category\",\n529\t          \"Gini (mean)\",\n530\t          \"Entropy (mean)\",\n531\t          \"Top-1 judge ASR fraction\"\n532\t        ],\n533\t        \"rows\": [\n534\t          [\n535\t            \"prompt_injection\",\n536\t            \"targeted\",\n537\t            \"0.82\",\n538\t            \"0.73\",\n539\t            \"0.65\"\n540\t          ],\n541\t          [\n542\t            \"score_manipulation\",\n543\t            \"targeted\",\n544\t            \"0.79\",\n545\t            \"0.78\",\n546\t            \"0.62\"\n547\t          ],\n548\t          [\n549\t            \"position_bias\",\n550\t            \"targeted\",\n551\t            \"0.74\",\n552\t            \"0.94\",\n553\t            \"0.56\"\n554\t          ],\n555\t          [\n556\t            \"sycophancy\",\n557\t            \"shared-bias\",\n558\t            \"0.45\",\n559\t            \"1.38\",\n560\t            \"0.40\"\n561\t          ],\n562\t          [\n563\t            \"verbosity_bias\",\n564\t            \"shared-bias\",\n565\t            \"0.42\",\n566\t            \"1.47\",\n567\t            \"0.37\"\n568\t          ],\n569\t          [\n570\t            \"authority_bias\",\n571\t            \"shared-bias\",\n572\t            \"0.41\",\n573\t            \"1.50\",\n574\t            \"0.36\"\n575\t          ]\n576\t        ]\n577\t      }\n578\t    ],\n579\t    \"figures\": [],\n580\t    \"analysis\": \"ASR 浓度分析为 η_max 主导性提供了微观机制证据，超越了回归系数的间接推断。审稿人常问 \\\"what's the mechanism?\\\"——本实验直接回答：targeted adversary 将攻击集中在 weakest judge 上（Gini>0.7），使 η_max 成为 panel 脆弱性的充分统计量。shared-bias 下 ASR 更分散 解释了为什么 K_eff 在这类攻击中为负——diversity 提供 partial immunity 因为并非所有 judges 都同样受 shared bias 影响。此发现独立验证 GAM taxonomy。\\n\\nTargeted attacks（prompt injection, score manipulation, position bias）利用特定 judge 的个体弱点——adversary 的攻击策略集中在 panel 中最脆弱的 judge 上。这导致 ASR 分布 高度集中（Gini 0.72-0.85）：top-1 judge 贡献了约 61% 的 panel 总 ASR。这是 η_max 主导性的直接微观机制证据——vulnerability 确实集中在 weakest link。相比之下，shared-bias attacks（sycophancy, verbosity, authority）利用多个 judges 共享的认知偏差，ASR 更 均匀地分布在 panel 成员间（Gini 0.35-0.52），top-1 judge 仅贡献约 38%。Gini 与 η_max 的高相关（r=0.83）直接证明 panel-level vulnerability 与 judge-level concentration 是同一现象的两个面。这为 GAM 6:6 split 提供了独立的 mechanistic 验证——targeted 和 shared-bias 不仅在 K_eff 方向上分裂，在 ASR concentration 模式上也完全分裂。\"\n581\t  },\n582\t  {\n583\t    \"name\": \"Diversity-Capability Tradeoff Visualization\",\n584\t    \"description\": \"绘制 K_eff vs η_max scatter，拟合 tradeoff curve，计算 Pareto frontier，按 tier 分层\",\n585\t    \"results\": {\n586\t      \"overall_keff_etamax_r\": 0.7,\n587\t      \"overall_keff_etamax_r_ci95\": [\n588\t        0.66,\n589\t        0.74\n590\t      ],\n591\t      \"tier_stratified\": {\n592\t        \"base_tier_r\": 0.52,\n593\t        \"mid_tier_r\": 0.48,\n594\t        \"frontier_tier_r\": 0.35\n595\t      },\n596\t      \"pareto_frontier_size\": 12,\n597\t      \"pareto_dominance_pct\": \"97.4% of panels dominated\",\n598\t      \"pareto_frontier_composition\": \"predominantly low-K_eff, low-η_max panels\",\n599\t      \"tradeoff_curve_fit\": \"monotone increasing, concave\",\n600\t      \"within_family_r\": 0.81,\n601\t      \"cross_family_r\": 0.65\n602\t    },\n603\t    \"tables\": [\n604\t      {\n605\t        \"name\": \"Tradeoff Correlation by Stratification\",\n606\t        \"columns\": [\n607\t          \"Stratification\",\n608\t          \"N panels\",\n609\t          \"r(K_eff, η_max)\",\n610\t          \"95% CI\"\n611\t        ],\n612\t        \"rows\": [\n613\t          [\n614\t            \"Full pool\",\n615\t            \"455\",\n616\t            \"0.70\",\n617\t            \"[0.66, 0.74]\"\n618\t          ],\n619\t          [\n620\t            \"Base tier only\",\n621\t            \"84\",\n622\t            \"0.52\",\n623\t            \"[0.38, 0.64]\"\n624\t          ],\n625\t          [\n626\t            \"Within-family\",\n627\t            \"varies\",\n628\t            \"0.81\",\n629\t            \"[0.73, 0.87]\"\n630\t          ],\n631\t          [\n632\t            \"Cross-family\",\n633\t            \"varies\",\n634\t            \"0.65\",\n635\t            \"[0.58, 0.71]\"\n636\t          ]\n637\t        ]\n638\t      }\n639\t    ],\n640\t    \"figures\": [],\n641\t    \"analysis\": \"可视化使 structural constraint 具象化——审稿人直观理解为什么 max_keff 策略失败（右上角） 而 min_eta_max 策略成功（左下角）。Tier 内相关降低的发现为 two-stage algorithm 提供了 理论基础：capability screening 打破了跨 tier 的 strong tradeoff，使后续 diversity 优化在弱 tradeoff 条件下进行。此 figure 应作为论文 Fig 3 或 Fig 4。\\n\\nr=0.70 的 structural correlation 源于当前 LLM 生态系统的特性：最大化 K_eff 需要包含来自 不同 capability tiers 的模型（不同 family × tier 组合提供最大 behavioral diversity）， 这必然引入能力较弱的 judges，推高 η_max。Tier 分层后 r 降低（base: 0.52, frontier: 0.35） 说明 tradeoff 在 tier 内较弱——within tier 的 diversity（来自不同 architecture/training） 不需要大幅牺牲 capability。这支持 two-stage recommendation 的逻辑：先筛选 capability tier（打破跨 tier tradeoff），再在 tier 内最大化 diversity（利用弱化的 within-tier tradeoff）。 Pareto frontier 几乎全部由 low-K_eff, low-η_max panels 占据——no free lunch，但 robustness-first selection 自然落在 Pareto frontier 上。\"\n642\t  },\n643\t  {\n644\t    \"name\": \"Panel Size Sensitivity Analysis\",\n645\t    \"description\": \"测试 K=3,5,7,9 不同 panel 尺寸下 η_max 主导性是否持续\",\n646\t    \"results\": {\n647\t      \"panel_sizes\": [\n648\t        3,\n649\t        5,\n650\t        7,\n651\t        9\n652\t      ],\n653\t      \"panels_per_size\": [\n654\t        455,\n655\t        3003,\n656\t        6435,\n657\t        5005\n658\t      ],\n659\t      \"eta_max_sig_by_k_clustered_se\": {\n660\t        \"k3\": \"8/12\",\n661\t        \"k5\": \"9/12\",\n662\t        \"k7\": \"9/12\",\n663\t        \"k9\": \"8/12\"\n664\t      },\n665\t      \"keff_sig_by_k_clustered_se\": {\n666\t        \"k3\": \"0/12\",\n667\t        \"k5\": \"1/12\",\n668\t        \"k7\": \"1/12\",\n669\t        \"k9\": \"2/12\"\n670\t      },\n671\t      \"dominance_ratio_by_k\": {\n672\t        \"k3\": \"8:0\",\n673\t        \"k5\": \"9:1\",\n674\t        \"k7\": \"9:1\",\n675\t        \"k9\": \"4:1\"\n676\t      },\n677\t      \"eta_max_effect_size_trend\": \"decreasing with K (from 0.42 at K=3 to 0.31 at K=9)\",\n678\t      \"keff_effect_size_trend\": \"stable (0.12-0.16 across all K)\",\n679\t      \"min_eta_max_wins_by_k\": {\n680\t        \"k3\": \"12/12\",\n681\t        \"k5\": \"12/12\",\n682\t        \"k7\": \"12/12\",\n683\t        \"k9\": \"12/12\"\n684\t      },\n685\t      \"se_inflation_by_k\": [\n686\t        2.5,\n687\t        4.1,\n688\t        6.3,\n689\t        7.8\n690\t      ]\n691\t    },\n692\t    \"tables\": [\n693\t      {\n694\t        \"name\": \"Panel Size Sensitivity Summary (Clustered SE)\",\n695\t        \"columns\": [\n696\t          \"K\",\n697\t          \"Panels\",\n698\t          \"η_max sig\",\n699\t          \"K_eff sig\",\n700\t          \"Ratio\",\n701\t          \"SE inflation\",\n702\t          \"η_max β (mean)\"\n703\t        ],\n704\t        \"rows\": [\n705\t          [\n706\t            \"3\",\n707\t            \"455\",\n708\t            \"8/12\",\n709\t            \"0/12\",\n710\t            \"8:0\",\n711\t            \"2.5x\",\n712\t            \"0.42\"\n713\t          ],\n714\t          [\n715\t            \"5\",\n716\t            \"3003\",\n717\t            \"9/12\",\n718\t            \"1/12\",\n719\t            \"9:1\",\n720\t            \"4.1x\",\n721\t            \"0.38\"\n722\t          ],\n723\t          [\n724\t            \"7\",\n725\t            \"6435\",\n726\t            \"9/12\",\n727\t            \"1/12\",\n728\t            \"9:1\",\n729\t            \"6.3x\",\n730\t            \"0.34\"\n731\t          ],\n732\t          [\n733\t            \"9\",\n734\t            \"5005\",\n735\t            \"8/12\",\n736\t            \"2/12\",\n737\t            \"4:1\",\n738\t            \"7.8x\",\n739\t            \"0.31\"\n740\t          ]\n741\t        ]\n742\t      }\n743\t    ],\n744\t    \"figures\": [],\n745\t    \"analysis\": \"Panel size sensitivity 提供两个关键发现：(1) η_max 主导性在 K=3 到 K=9 范围内稳定持续， 确认 weakest-link 不是小 panel 的 artifact；(2) SE 膨胀随 K 急剧增加，为方法论 contribution（non-independence correction 的必要性）提供量化支撑。K=9 时 K_eff 达到 2/12 显著但 effect size 仍微小——power 增加检测到了真实但 practically insignificant 的效应。论文 supplementary 中可报告此分析作为 robustness check。\\n\\nη_max 主导性在所有 K 下持续因为 weakest-link 机制是 scale-invariant：无论 panel 有多少 judges，adversary 总是针对最脆弱的那个。K 增加时 η_max 的 effect size 略降（0.42→0.31） 因为更大 panel 中 majority vote 的容错能力增加——单个 judge 的失败更难翻转整个 panel。 但 η_max 仍然主导，因为 adversary 不只针对一个 judge——adaptive adversary 可以同时攻击 多个弱 judges。K_eff 在 K=9 时达到 2/12 显著：更多 panels（5005）提供了更多统计 power， 但 effect size 保持微小（0.12-0.16）。SE 膨胀随 K 急剧增加（每个 model 出现在更多 panels 中），从 K=3 的 2.5x 到 K=9 的 7.8x。这为 non-independence 校正方法的必要性 提供了更强的论据——在 K=7 或 K=9 下使用 OLS 会产生极度膨胀的显著性计数。 min_eta_max 策略在所有 K 下赢 12/12，确认 practical recommendation 对 panel size 鲁棒。\"\n746\t  },\n747\t  {\n748\t    \"name\": \"VIF + Multicollinearity Diagnostic\",\n749\t    \"description\": \"计算 VIF、partial correlations、residualized K_eff regression，应用 Bonferroni/FDR 校正，尝试 beta regression\",\n750\t    \"results\": {\n751\t      \"gpu_needed\": false,\n752\t      \"raw_vif_keff\": 2.96,\n753\t      \"raw_vif_eta_max\": 2.96,\n754\t      \"residualized_vif_keff\": 1.0,\n755\t      \"partial_correlation_keff_asr_given_eta\": 0.18,\n756\t      \"partial_correlation_eta_asr_given_keff\": 0.42,\n757\t      \"bonferroni_eta_max_sig\": \"7/12\",\n758\t      \"bonferroni_keff_sig\": \"2/12\",\n759\t      \"fdr_eta_max_sig\": \"8/12\",\n760\t      \"fdr_keff_sig\": \"3/12\",\n761\t      \"beta_regression_eta_max_sig\": \"10/12\",\n762\t      \"beta_regression_keff_sig\": \"4/12 (3+/1-)\",\n763\t      \"beta_regression_dispersion_phi\": [\n764\t        3.2,\n765\t        8.7\n766\t      ],\n767\t      \"condition_number\": 4.8,\n768\t      \"reviewer_blocking_issue\": false\n769\t    },\n770\t    \"tables\": [\n771\t      {\n772\t        \"name\": \"Multicollinearity Diagnostics\",\n773\t        \"columns\": [\n774\t          \"Metric\",\n775\t          \"Value\",\n776\t          \"Threshold\",\n777\t          \"Status\"\n778\t        ],\n779\t        \"rows\": [\n780\t          [\n781\t            \"VIF (K_eff, raw)\",\n782\t            \"2.96\",\n783\t            \"< 5 (strict) / < 10 (standard)\",\n784\t            \"PASS\"\n785\t          ],\n786\t          [\n787\t            \"VIF (K_eff, residualized)\",\n788\t            \"1.00\",\n789\t            \"< 5\",\n790\t            \"PASS\"\n791\t          ],\n792\t          [\n793\t            \"Condition number\",\n794\t            \"4.8\",\n795\t            \"< 30\",\n796\t            \"PASS\"\n797\t          ],\n798\t          [\n799\t            \"Partial r(K_eff, ASR | η_max)\",\n800\t            \"0.18\",\n801\t            \"-\",\n802\t            \"Weak\"\n803\t          ],\n804\t          [\n805\t            \"Partial r(η_max, ASR | K_eff)\",\n806\t            \"0.42\",\n807\t            \"-\",\n808\t            \"Moderate-strong\"\n809\t          ]\n810\t        ]\n811\t      },\n812\t      {\n813\t        \"name\": \"Method Comparison with Multiple Testing Correction\",\n814\t        \"columns\": [\n815\t          \"Method\",\n816\t          \"η_max sig\",\n817\t          \"K_eff sig\",\n818\t          \"K_eff direction\"\n819\t        ],\n820\t        \"rows\": [\n821\t          [\n822\t            \"OLS + FDR\",\n823\t            \"11/12\",\n824\t            \"8/12\",\n825\t            \"7+/1-\"\n826\t          ],\n827\t          [\n828\t            \"OLS + Bonferroni\",\n829\t            \"7/12\",\n830\t            \"2/12\",\n831\t            \"2+/0-\"\n832\t          ],\n833\t          [\n834\t            \"Clustered SE + FDR\",\n835\t            \"8/12\",\n836\t            \"0/12\",\n837\t            \"-\"\n838\t          ],\n839\t          [\n840\t            \"Beta regression + FDR\",\n841\t            \"10/12\",\n842\t            \"4/12\",\n843\t            \"3+/1-\"\n844\t          ]\n845\t        ]\n846\t      }\n847\t    ],\n848\t    \"figures\": [],\n849\t    \"analysis\": \"VIF 分析消除了审稿人 RC1 的 last-resort 攻击角度——multicollinearity is moderate, not pathological。r=0.70 在经验社会科学中常见（e.g., income and education）， standard practice 是报告 VIF 并继续。Beta regression 提供了 distributional robustness check：结论与 log-log OLS 一致。论文可在 methods 节用一段话报告 VIF diagnostics 并在 supplementary 中给出完整表格。\\n\\nRaw VIF ≈ 2.96 直接由 r=0.70 的 confound 决定（VIF = 1/(1-r²) = 1/(1-0.49) = 1.96 在 bivariate 情况下；加上 tier indicators 后升至约 2.96）。VIF < 5 远低于标准 reviewer concern 阈值（通常 VIF > 10），甚至低于 stricter 标准（VIF > 5）。Residualization 后 VIF 降至 1.0（by construction），residualized K_eff 的 partial correlation 仅 0.18 vs η_max 的 0.42——直接量化了主导性差异。Beta regression 作为 ASR ∈ [0,1] 的 distributional 替代方案：η_max 显著性从 log-log OLS 的 11/12 降至 10/12（beta regression 对极端值更鲁棒），K_eff 从 8/12 升至 4/12（beta regression 更好地处理 heteroscedasticity）。Condition number 4.8 < 30 确认无有害多重共线性。Bonferroni 校正（most conservative）给出 η_max 7/12 vs K_eff 2/12——即使在最保守的多重比较 校正下 η_max 仍显著主导。无 reviewer-blocking issue。\"\n850\t  },\n851\t  {\n852\t    \"name\": \"Aggregation Gradient Under Clustered SE\",\n853\t    \"description\": \"在 clustered SE 和 bootstrap 下重新运行 4 种聚合规则 + 新增 veto rule，验证聚合梯度是否为真实效应而非 overlap 伪迹\",\n854\t    \"results\": {\n855\t      \"aggregation_rules\": [\n856\t        \"majority\",\n857\t        \"weighted\",\n858\t        \"threshold\",\n859\t        \"bayesian\",\n860\t        \"veto\"\n861\t      ],\n862\t      \"correction_methods\": [\n863\t        \"OLS\",\n864\t        \"clustered_se\",\n865\t        \"bootstrap_v2\"\n866\t      ],\n867\t      \"majority_clustered_se\": {\n868\t        \"eta_sig\": \"8/12\",\n869\t        \"keff_sig\": \"0/12\"\n870\t      },\n871\t      \"weighted_clustered_se\": {\n872\t        \"eta_sig\": \"6/12\",\n873\t        \"keff_sig\": \"1/12\",\n874\t        \"keff_direction\": \"1+\"\n875\t      },\n876\t      \"threshold_clustered_se\": {\n877\t        \"eta_sig\": \"10/12\",\n878\t        \"keff_sig\": \"4/12\",\n879\t        \"keff_direction\": \"3+/1-\",\n880\t        \"r2\": 0.87\n881\t      },\n882\t      \"bayesian_clustered_se\": {\n883\t        \"eta_sig\": \"5/12\",\n884\t        \"keff_sig\": \"4/12\",\n885\t        \"keff_direction\": \"1+/3-\",\n886\t        \"keff_negative_frac\": \"3/4\"\n887\t      },\n888\t      \"veto_clustered_se\": {\n889\t        \"eta_sig\": \"11/12\",\n890\t        \"keff_sig\": \"0/12\",\n891\t        \"r2\": 0.82\n892\t      },\n893\t      \"bayesian_bootstrap\": {\n894\t        \"eta_sig\": \"3/12\",\n895\t        \"keff_sig\": \"3/12\",\n896\t        \"keff_direction\": \"0+/3-\",\n897\t        \"keff_negative_frac\": \"3/3\"\n898\t      },\n899\t      \"gradient_preserved_under_correction\": true,\n900\t      \"bayesian_keff_flip_genuine\": true,\n901\t      \"aggregation_gradient_order\": \"veto > threshold > majority > weighted > bayesian\"\n902\t    },\n903\t    \"tables\": [\n904\t      {\n905\t        \"name\": \"Aggregation Gradient Under Clustered SE\",\n906\t        \"columns\": [\n907\t          \"Rule\",\n908\t          \"η_max sig\",\n909\t          \"K_eff sig\",\n910\t          \"K_eff neg frac\",\n911\t          \"R²\",\n912\t          \"Gradient position\"\n913\t        ],\n914\t        \"rows\": [\n915\t          [\n916\t            \"Veto\",\n917\t            \"11/12\",\n918\t            \"0/12\",\n919\t            \"-\",\n920\t            \"0.82\",\n921\t            \"Maximum vulnerability\"\n922\t          ],\n923\t          [\n924\t            \"Threshold\",\n925\t            \"10/12\",\n926\t            \"4/12\",\n927\t            \"1/4\",\n928\t            \"0.87\",\n929\t            \"High\"\n930\t          ],\n931\t          [\n932\t            \"Majority\",\n933\t            \"8/12\",\n934\t            \"0/12\",\n935\t            \"-\",\n936\t            \"0.28\",\n937\t            \"Moderate\"\n938\t          ],\n939\t          [\n940\t            \"Weighted\",\n941\t            \"6/12\",\n942\t            \"1/12\",\n943\t            \"0/1\",\n944\t            \"0.26\",\n945\t            \"Low-moderate\"\n946\t          ],\n947\t          [\n948\t            \"Bayesian\",\n949\t            \"5/12\",\n950\t            \"4/12\",\n951\t            \"3/4\",\n952\t            \"0.09\",\n953\t            \"Minimum vulnerability\"\n954\t          ]\n955\t        ]\n956\t      },\n957\t      {\n958\t        \"name\": \"Bayesian K_eff Direction Detail\",\n959\t        \"columns\": [\n960\t          \"Correction\",\n961\t          \"K_eff sig total\",\n962\t          \"K_eff positive\",\n963\t          \"K_eff negative\",\n964\t          \"Neg fraction\"\n965\t        ],\n966\t        \"rows\": [\n967\t          [\n968\t            \"OLS\",\n969\t            \"7/12\",\n970\t            \"1\",\n971\t            \"6\",\n972\t            \"6/7 (86%)\"\n973\t          ],\n974\t          [\n975\t            \"Clustered SE\",\n976\t            \"4/12\",\n977\t            \"1\",\n978\t            \"3\",\n979\t            \"3/4 (75%)\"\n980\t          ],\n981\t          [\n982\t            \"Bootstrap v2\",\n983\t            \"3/12\",\n984\t            \"0\",\n985\t            \"3\",\n986\t            \"3/3 (100%)\"\n987\t          ]\n988\t        ]\n989\t      }\n990\t    ],\n991\t    \"figures\": [],\n992\t    \"analysis\": \"聚合梯度在校正下的稳健性是论文的独立贡献——它不受 non-independence concern 的影响，因为 它描述的是投票规则数学的 structural 性质。Veto rule 的加入使梯度两端更 extreme： veto（pure weakest-link）vs Bayesian（weakest-link neutralized + diversity flip）。 论文可以将此呈现为 defense design spectrum——practitioners 根据其对 false positive vs false negative 的偏好选择适当位置。Bayesian K_eff 在 bootstrap 下 3/3 negative 是 cleanest possible evidence for the flip。\\n\\n聚合梯度在 clustered SE 下保持，因为不同投票规则产生的脆弱性差异是 structural/mathematical 的，不是 panel overlap 的伪迹。Threshold（unanimity）要求所有 judges 一致，使单个 judge 的 failure 直接传导为 panel failure——R²=0.87 说明 panel 结构几乎完全决定了 threshold voting 下的脆弱性。这种强 structural 效应在 clustered SE 下大量存活（η_max 10/12, K_eff 4/12）。Veto rule（单个 judge 可否决）是 weakest-link 的极端化——η_max 几乎 完美预测（11/12），K_eff 被完全压倒（0/12）。 Bayesian calibration 翻转 K_eff 方向的关键机制：Bayesian 使用 prior accuracy 下调不可靠 judges 的权重，有效中和了 weakest-link 通道。η_max 的直接效应被削弱（11→5/12）。 剩余的 K_eff 信号主要来自 shared-bias 条件（diversity 保护性的部分），因此净方向为负。 在 bootstrap 下，Bayesian K_eff 仅 3/12 显著但全部为负（3/3 negative fraction）—— direction flip 是真实的。这确认 aggregation 是独立于 non-independence correction 的 control lever。论文的 prescriptive conclusion（robustness-first + Bayesian = dual-channel defense）在最严格校正下依然成立。\"\n993\t  },\n994\t  {\n995\t    \"name\": \"Open-Ended Generation Benchmark Extension\",\n996\t    \"description\": \"在 MT-Bench 风格的 open-ended generation 任务上测试 weakest-link 假说，超越 MCQ 格式\",\n997\t    \"results\": {\n998\t      \"benchmark\": \"MT-Bench (8 categories)\",\n999\t      \"judge_format\": \"1-10 scale scoring\",\n1000\t      \"models_available\": 12,\n1001\t      \"panels\": 220,\n1002\t      \"attack_types\": [\n1003\t        \"style_manipulation\",\n1004\t        \"length_inflation\",\n1005\t        \"format_gaming\"\n1006\t      ],\n1007\t      \"conditions\": 6,\n1008\t      \"eta_max_sig_ols\": \"5/6\",\n1009\t      \"keff_sig_ols\": \"3/6 (2+/1-)\",\n1010\t      \"eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"4/6\",\n1011\t      \"keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/6\",\n1012\t      \"r2_mean\": 0.22,\n1013\t      \"gam_generation_split\": {\n1014\t        \"style_manipulation\": \"shared-bias (negative K_eff)\",\n1015\t        \"length_inflation\": \"shared-bias (negative K_eff)\",\n1016\t        \"format_gaming\": \"targeted (positive K_eff)\"\n1017\t      },\n1018\t      \"min_eta_max_wins\": \"6/6\",\n1019\t      \"cross_format_consistency\": \"η_max dominant in both MCQ and generation\"\n1020\t    },\n1021\t    \"tables\": [\n1022\t      {\n1023\t        \"name\": \"Generation Benchmark Results (Clustered SE)\",\n1024\t        \"columns\": [\n1025\t          \"Condition\",\n1026\t          \"η_max sig?\",\n1027\t          \"K_eff sig?\",\n1028\t          \"K_eff GAM dir\",\n1029\t          \"R²\"\n1030\t        ],\n1031\t        \"rows\": [\n1032\t          [\n1033\t            \"style_manipulation × MT-Bench\",\n1034\t            \"Yes\",\n1035\t            \"No\",\n1036\t            \"negative\",\n1037\t            \"0.19\"\n1038\t          ],\n1039\t          [\n1040\t            \"length_inflation × MT-Bench\",\n1041\t            \"Yes\",\n1042\t            \"No\",\n1043\t            \"negative\",\n1044\t            \"0.24\"\n1045\t          ],\n1046\t          [\n1047\t            \"format_gaming × MT-Bench\",\n1048\t            \"Yes\",\n1049\t            \"No\",\n1050\t            \"positive\",\n1051\t            \"0.23\"\n1052\t          ]\n1053\t        ]\n1054\t      },\n1055\t      {\n1056\t        \"name\": \"Cross-Format Consistency\",\n1057\t        \"columns\": [\n1058\t          \"Format\",\n1059\t          \"η_max sig (CL-SE)\",\n1060\t          \"K_eff sig (CL-SE)\",\n1061\t          \"Dominance ratio\"\n1062\t        ],\n1063\t        \"rows\": [\n1064\t          [\n1065\t            \"MCQ (MMLU+ARC)\",\n1066\t            \"8/12\",\n1067\t            \"0/12\",\n1068\t            \"8:0\"\n1069\t          ],\n1070\t          [\n1071\t            \"Generation (MT-Bench)\",\n1072\t            \"4/6\",\n1073\t            \"0/6\",\n1074\t            \"4:0\"\n1075\t          ],\n1076\t          [\n1077\t            \"Combined\",\n1078\t            \"12/18\",\n1079\t            \"0/18\",\n1080\t            \"12:0\"\n1081\t          ]\n1082\t        ]\n1083\t      }\n1084\t    ],\n1085\t    \"figures\": [],\n1086\t    \"analysis\": \"Generation extension 消除了\\\"MCQ-specific artifact\\\"的审稿人质疑。η_max 主导性跨 task format 通用性是论文 generalizability 论证的关键证据。R² 降低反映了 generation evaluation 的内在 noise，但 relative driver importance（η_max >> K_eff）完全保持。 此实验可作为 Section 5 的扩展分析或 supplementary material。\\n\\nη_max 主导性在 generation 任务中持续因为底层机制相同：无论 judges 评估 MCQ 正确性还是 generation 质量，adversary 都针对最可操纵的 judge。Generation 的 1-10 scale 提供了比 MCQ binary 更多的操纵空间（微妙的 style/format manipulation 可以影响 rubric-based scoring），但 vulnerability 的 distribution across judges 仍然是高度不均匀的—— 某些 judges 对 length inflation 或 format gaming 特别敏感。R² 较低（0.22 vs MCQ 的 0.30）因为 generation evaluation 有更多 idiosyncratic variance（rubric interpretation, 文化偏好等）。K_eff 在 OLS 下 3/6 显著但 clustered SE 后归零——与 MCQ 完全一致。 GAM 分类中，style manipulation 和 length inflation 属于 shared-bias（所有 LLM judges 都倾向于给更长/更 polished 的回答更高分），而 format gaming 属于 targeted（利用特定 model 的 format parsing 差异）。12 模型（部分 API 模型不支持 generation evaluation） 给出 220 panels，足够进行 regression analysis。min_eta_max 策略在 generation 上同样 赢 6/6，确认 practical recommendation 跨 task format 通用。\"\n1087\t  },\n1088\t  {\n1089\t    \"name\": \"Partial-Knowledge Adversary Model\",\n1090\t    \"description\": \"模拟 adversary 仅知道 judge family labels（不知具体脆弱性 profile）的 realistic threat model\",\n1091\t    \"results\": {\n1092\t      \"knowledge_levels\": [\n1093\t        \"full (baseline)\",\n1094\t        \"family-only\",\n1095\t        \"random\"\n1096\t      ],\n1097\t      \"asr_reduction_family_vs_full_pct\": 18,\n1098\t      \"asr_reduction_random_vs_full_pct\": 42,\n1099\t      \"family_knowledge_eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"7/12\",\n1100\t      \"family_knowledge_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/12\",\n1101\t      \"family_knowledge_dominance_ratio\": \"7:0\",\n1102\t      \"random_targeting_eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"3/12\",\n1103\t      \"random_targeting_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/12\",\n1104\t      \"family_knowledge_r2_mean\": 0.24,\n1105\t      \"family_label_attack_efficiency\": 0.82\n1106\t    },\n1107\t    \"tables\": [\n1108\t      {\n1109\t        \"name\": \"Adversary Knowledge Level Comparison (Clustered SE)\",\n1110\t        \"columns\": [\n1111\t          \"Knowledge level\",\n1112\t          \"Mean ASR\",\n1113\t          \"ASR vs full (%)\",\n1114\t          \"η_max sig\",\n1115\t          \"K_eff sig\",\n1116\t          \"R²\"\n1117\t        ],\n1118\t        \"rows\": [\n1119\t          [\n1120\t            \"Full knowledge\",\n1121\t            \"0.195\",\n1122\t            \"100%\",\n1123\t            \"8/12\",\n1124\t            \"0/12\",\n1125\t            \"0.30\"\n1126\t          ],\n1127\t          [\n1128\t            \"Family-only\",\n1129\t            \"0.160\",\n1130\t            \"82%\",\n1131\t            \"7/12\",\n1132\t            \"0/12\",\n1133\t            \"0.24\"\n1134\t          ],\n1135\t          [\n1136\t            \"Random\",\n1137\t            \"0.113\",\n1138\t            \"58%\",\n1139\t            \"3/12\",\n1140\t            \"0/12\",\n1141\t            \"0.08\"\n1142\t          ]\n1143\t        ]\n1144\t      },\n1145\t      {\n1146\t        \"name\": \"Family Label Informativeness\",\n1147\t        \"columns\": [\n1148\t          \"Metric\",\n1149\t          \"Value\",\n1150\t          \"Interpretation\"\n1151\t        ],\n1152\t        \"rows\": [\n1153\t          [\n1154\t            \"Attack efficiency (family/full)\",\n1155\t            \"0.82\",\n1156\t            \"Family labels highly informative for targeting\"\n1157\t          ],\n1158\t          [\n1159\t            \"Family-vulnerability correlation\",\n1160\t            \"0.61\",\n1161\t            \"Moderate; same family shares weaknesses\"\n1162\t          ],\n1163\t          [\n1164\t            \"η_max sig retention (family vs full)\",\n1165\t            \"7/8\",\n1166\t            \"Targeting still exploits weakest link\"\n1167\t          ]\n1168\t        ]\n1169\t      }\n1170\t    ],\n1171\t    \"figures\": [],\n1172\t    \"analysis\": \"Partial-knowledge 实验将论文结论从 worst-case（omniscient adversary）扩展至 realistic threat model。Family-only adversary 保留 82% 攻击效率这一发现对 practical defense implications 至关重要——defenders 不能依赖\\\"adversary 不知道 panel 具体组成\\\"的假设， 因为 family-level knowledge 几乎 sufficient。η_max 在所有 knowledge levels 下主导， K_eff 在所有 knowledge levels 下为 0/12——核心发现对 adversary 能力假设鲁棒。 Random targeting 的 R²=0.08 呼应 plan_003 的 RF 结论：panel 结构的预测力依赖于 adversary 的 strategic targeting——这是论文 adaptive vs random 对比叙事的第三个 independent evidence line。\\n\\nFamily-only adversary 的 ASR 仅降 18%（而非 random 的 42%），因为 family labels 与 vulnerability profiles 有中等相关：同 family 模型共享 training pipeline 和 architectural biases，adversary 可基于 family 推断出 approximately correct 的攻击 策略。η_max 仍然主导（7/12 vs full-knowledge 的 8/12）因为 family-level targeting 仍 preferentially hits weaker judges——family labels 虽然 noisy 但 informationally above chance。K_eff 在 partial-knowledge 下同样为 0/12——diversity 在任何 knowledge level 下都不是 independent protective factor after correction。Attack efficiency 0.82 意味着 family labels 提供了 82% of full-knowledge targeting effectiveness——这对 ecological validity 至关重要：现实中 adversary 通常知道 panel 的 model families （从 API endpoint, response style 等推断），因此 full-knowledge 结果的 relevance 不仅限于理论上限。Random targeting 下 η_max 仅 3/12 显著——random adversary 无法有效 利用 individual weaknesses，说明 η_max 的 predictive power 依赖于 adversary 的 targeting ability，与 adaptive vs RF contrast（plan_003）形成完整呼应。\"\n1173\t  }\n1174\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca7c92ca-7226-4597-b435-bb7be4a94344","uuid":"611f301a-6777-43fe-8ca4-7c7b62c91e1f","timestamp":"2026-05-22T22:36:25.722Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/cert_manip_resist_eval/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T221131/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"15-Model Scaling Expansion\",\n    \"description\": \"扩展至 15 模型（6 families），455 panels × 12 conditions 全量回归 + MI 矩阵 + 所有校正方法\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"DONE (plan001_step1_full_v4)\",\n      \"models\": 15,\n      \"panels\": 455,\n      \"conditions\": 12,\n      \"eta_max_sig_ols\": \"11/12\",\n      \"keff_sig_ols\": \"8/12 (7+/1-)\",\n      \"eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"8/12\",\n      \"keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/12\",\n      \"eta_max_sig_bootstrap_v2\": \"5/12\",\n      \"keff_sig_bootstrap_v2\": \"1/12\",\n      \"eta_max_sig_mixed_effects\": \"7/12\",\n      \"keff_sig_mixed_effects\": \"3/12\",\n      \"dominance_ratio_bootstrap\": \"5:1\",\n      \"gam_split\": \"6 targeted positive / 6 shared-bias negative\",\n      \"min_eta_max_wins\": \"12/12\",\n      \"confound_r\": 0.701,\n      \"se_inflation_factor\": \"~2.5x\",\n      \"rf_keff_sig\": \"2/2\",\n      \"rf_r2_mmlu\": 0.734,\n      \"rf_r2_arc\": 0.813\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Correction Method Comparison (Actual Results)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"η_max sig\",\n          \"K_eff sig\",\n          \"K_eff dir\",\n          \"Note\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"OLS\",\n            \"11/12\",\n            \"8/12\",\n            \"7+/1-\",\n            \"Panel overlap inflated\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Clustered SE (CR1, 15 clusters)\",\n            \"8/12\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"Conservative\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Wild cluster bootstrap v2\",\n            \"5/12\",\n            \"1/12\",\n            \"1+\",\n            \"Max-p across 3 positions\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mixed effects\",\n            \"7/12\",\n            \"3/12\",\n            \"3+\",\n            \"Random judge intercepts\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"已完成。η_max:K_eff 主导比从 OLS 的 1.4:1 升至 bootstrap 的 5:1，证明相对主导性在校正下 增强而非减弱。Benchmark 不对称（MMLU 4/6 vs ARC 1/6 存活 bootstrap）由 MMLU 4-choice 格式提供更多 scoring variance 解释。此结果构成 paper 的实证基础。\\n\\n已完成。15 模型覆盖 6 families × 3 capability tiers，提供 η_max 和 K_eff 充足方差。 SE 膨胀 ~2.5x 与 91/455 panel overlap 一致（claude-3-haiku 出现在 91 个 panels 中）。 η_max 存活校正因为它捕捉的是真实的个体 judge 脆弱性——不是 panel 重叠伪迹。 K_eff 崩溃因为其 OLS 显著性被 overlapping panels 的相关残差膨胀——clustered SE 控制共享 judge 成员关系后，K_eff 的独立信号太弱。GAM 6:6 分割源于攻击机制差异： targeted attacks 利用 judge 特异性弱点（diversity = 更多攻击面），shared-bias attacks 利用共性认知偏差（diversity = 部分 judges 免疫）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Attack Surface Expansion\",\n    \"description\": \"新增 3 种攻击类型（few-shot hijacking, persona manipulation, instruction override），在 15 模型 × 2 benchmarks 上运行，共 6 新 conditions\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"new_attack_types\": 3,\n      \"new_conditions\": 6,\n      \"total_conditions\": 18,\n      \"new_eta_max_sig_ols\": \"6/6\",\n      \"new_keff_sig_ols\": \"4/6 (3+/1-)\",\n      \"new_eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"5/6\",\n      \"new_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/6\",\n      \"new_eta_max_sig_bootstrap\": \"3/6\",\n      \"new_keff_sig_bootstrap\": \"0/6\",\n      \"combined_eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"13/18\",\n      \"combined_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/18\",\n      \"combined_dominance_ratio_clustered_se\": \"13:0\",\n      \"gam_extended_split\": \"10 targeted positive / 8 shared-bias negative\",\n      \"gam_new_attacks_classification\": {\n        \"few_shot_hijacking\": \"targeted (positive K_eff)\",\n        \"persona_manipulation\": \"shared-bias (negative K_eff)\",\n        \"instruction_override\": \"targeted (positive K_eff)\"\n      },\n      \"new_r2_range\": [\n        0.22,\n        0.45\n      ],\n      \"min_eta_max_wins_extended\": \"18/18\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Extended Attack Taxonomy (Clustered SE)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Attack Type\",\n          \"Mechanism\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"η_max sig?\",\n          \"K_eff sig?\",\n          \"K_eff GAM direction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"few-shot hijacking\",\n            \"targeted\",\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"positive\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"few-shot hijacking\",\n            \"targeted\",\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"positive\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"persona manipulation\",\n            \"shared-bias\",\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"negative\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"persona manipulation\",\n            \"shared-bias\",\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"negative\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"instruction override\",\n            \"targeted\",\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"positive\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"instruction override\",\n            \"targeted\",\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"positive\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Extended GAM Split Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Category\",\n          \"Original (6 attacks)\",\n          \"New (3 attacks)\",\n          \"Total\",\n          \"K_eff direction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Targeted\",\n            \"6/6 positive\",\n            \"4/4 positive\",\n            \"10/10\",\n            \"positive (diversity harmful)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Shared-bias\",\n            \"6/6 negative\",\n            \"2/2 negative (persona×2)\",\n            \"8/8\",\n            \"negative (diversity protective)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"新攻击类型提供独立证据线，确认 η_max 主导性不依赖于特定攻击选择。GAM taxonomy 从 6:6 扩展至 10:8，mechanistic split 的稳健性增强——审稿人无法再质疑 taxonomy 是 cherry-picked 6 种 攻击的巧合。Instruction override 在 ARC 上 η_max 未显著（ARC 2-choice 格式对 instruction override 的 judge 间方差不敏感），与原始 benchmark asymmetry 一致。论文标题和核心叙事完全支持。\\n\\nFew-shot hijacking 利用模型在 in-context learning 上的个体差异——不同 judges 对 few-shot 示例的敏感度差异极大（GPT-4.1 vs Llama-8B 可差 3-5x），因此属于 targeted attack，η_max 捕捉最易受影响的 judge。Instruction override 利用 instruction-following 能力的模型间方差， 同样属于 targeted。Persona manipulation 利用 LLMs 对权威/身份线索的普遍敏感性——这是一种 共享认知偏差，不同能力模型都会受影响，因此属于 shared-bias，K_eff 方向为负（diversity 提供 部分免疫）。新攻击在 OLS 下延续 η_max 主导模式，但 K_eff 再次因 panel overlap 膨胀而 显著——clustered SE 后归零，与原 12 conditions 完全一致。GAM 扩展至 10:8 分割，clean taxonomy 覆盖 9 种攻击类型。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Random-Fault BFT Contrast Experiment\",\n    \"description\": \"Monte Carlo 随机故障模拟作为 BFT 对照。每个 judge 以 η_j = 1 - clean_accuracy 独立失败，majority vote。对比 adaptive regime 证明 BFT 反转\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"regime\": \"Random Fault (i.i.d.)\",\n      \"conditions\": 2,\n      \"monte_carlo_iterations\": 10000,\n      \"rf_keff_sig_ols\": \"2/2\",\n      \"rf_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"2/2\",\n      \"rf_keff_sig_bootstrap\": \"2/2\",\n      \"rf_keff_direction\": \"positive (2/2)\",\n      \"rf_keff_std_beta_mmlu\": 0.215,\n      \"rf_keff_std_beta_arc\": 0.379,\n      \"rf_eta_sig_all_methods\": \"2/2\",\n      \"rf_r2_mmlu\": 0.78,\n      \"rf_r2_arc\": 0.81,\n      \"adaptive_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/12\",\n      \"adaptive_keff_sig_bootstrap\": \"1/12\",\n      \"delta_r2_rf_vs_adaptive\": 0.48,\n      \"go_nogo_gate\": \"PASS (RF K_eff ≥2/2)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RF vs Adaptive Contrast (Key Metrics)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Random Fault\",\n          \"Adaptive\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"K_eff sig (OLS)\",\n            \"2/2\",\n            \"8/12 (7+/1-)\",\n            \"Both appear significant under OLS\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K_eff sig (Clustered SE)\",\n            \"2/2\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"RF genuine; adaptive artifactual\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K_eff sig (Bootstrap v2)\",\n            \"2/2\",\n            \"1/12\",\n            \"Consistent contrast\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K_eff std β (mean)\",\n            \"+0.297\",\n            \"+0.164\",\n            \"RF effect larger and genuine\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"R²\",\n            \"0.78-0.81\",\n            \"0.25-0.35\",\n            \"RF structurally determined; adaptive not\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"η_max sig (all methods)\",\n            \"2/2\",\n            \"5-8/12\",\n            \"η_max genuine in both regimes\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RF Per-Benchmark Detail\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"η_max β\",\n          \"K_eff β\",\n          \"R²\",\n          \"K_eff p (bootstrap)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"+0.482\",\n            \"+0.215\",\n            \"0.78\",\n            \"0.003\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"+0.551\",\n            \"+0.379\",\n            \"0.81\",\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是论文的关键因果证据。RF 对照证明 K_eff 在满足 i.i.d. 假设时有真实效应——BFT 理论 在随机故障下成立。而 adaptive regime 下 K_eff 的 OLS 显著性完全是 panel overlap 的伪迹。 这不是\\\"diversity helps under RF but hurts under adaptive\\\"——K_eff 在两种 regime 下方向均 为正。区别是：RF 下 K_eff 的正关联是真实的（panel 结构决定了容错性），adaptive 下是膨胀的 （adversary 引入的策略方差使 panel 结构预测力崩溃）。此发现为 Contribution #2（BFT reversal evidence）提供了不可替代的因果论证。\\n\\n随机故障下 K_eff 显著的根本原因是 BFT 的 i.i.d. 假设成立：每个 judge 独立以固定概率犯错， panel 结构（多样性）直接影响冗余覆盖。K_eff 高的 panel 中 judges 的错误模式更不相关， majority vote 的容错能力与独立性成正比——这正是 BFT 的核心机制。K_eff 方向为正（diversity → higher error）因为高 K_eff panel 必然包含弱模型（r=0.70 tradeoff），而在 i.i.d. 体制下 弱模型的高错误率直接传导为 panel 错误率——但关键是 K_eff 的贡献是独立的、真实的（所有校正 方法均显著 2/2）。对照 adaptive regime：相同的 K_eff 在 OLS 下显著 8/12，但 clustered SE 后崩溃至 0/12——因为 adaptive adversary 引入了 panel 结构无法预测的策略方差，K_eff 的 apparent OLS 信号完全来自 panel overlap 膨胀。R² 差异（RF 0.78-0.81 vs adaptive ~0.30） 直接量化了 adaptive adversary 引入的不可预测性。GO/NO-GO gate 通过，BFT framing 得到 因果层面的支撑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Capability-Matched Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"在同一 capability tier 内（主要利用 9-model base tier, 84 panels）测试控制 η_max 方差后 K_eff 是否浮现为显著预测因子\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"primary_tier\": \"base (9 models, 84 panels)\",\n      \"within_tier_eta_max_variance_reduction\": \"65-70%\",\n      \"within_tier_keff_eta_max_r\": 0.35,\n      \"conditions\": 12,\n      \"within_tier_keff_sig_ols\": \"5/12\",\n      \"within_tier_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"2/12\",\n      \"within_tier_keff_direction\": \"4+/1-\",\n      \"within_tier_eta_max_sig_ols\": \"7/12\",\n      \"within_tier_eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"4/12\",\n      \"within_tier_dominance_ratio\": \"2:1\",\n      \"within_tier_r2_mean\": 0.18,\n      \"cross_tier_comparison\": {\n        \"full_pool_dominance_ratio\": \"5:1\",\n        \"within_tier_dominance_ratio\": \"2:1\",\n        \"interpretation\": \"η_max still dominant but K_eff gains relative signal\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-Tier vs Within-Tier Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Setting\",\n          \"Panels\",\n          \"K_eff-η_max r\",\n          \"η_max sig (CL-SE)\",\n          \"K_eff sig (CL-SE)\",\n          \"Ratio\",\n          \"R² mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Full pool (15 models)\",\n            \"455\",\n            \"0.70\",\n            \"8/12\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"8:0\",\n            \"0.30\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Base tier (9 models)\",\n            \"84\",\n            \"0.35\",\n            \"4/12\",\n            \"2/12\",\n            \"2:1\",\n            \"0.18\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Frontier tier (3 models)\",\n            \"1\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Within-Tier K_eff Significant Conditions\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"K_eff β\",\n          \"K_eff p (CL-SE)\",\n          \"Direction\",\n          \"GAM confirms?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"mmlu×prompt_injection\",\n            \"+0.31\",\n            \"0.028\",\n            \"positive\",\n            \"Yes (targeted)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mmlu×score_manipulation\",\n            \"+0.25\",\n            \"0.041\",\n            \"positive\",\n            \"Yes (targeted)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Capability-matched validation 提供了 disentangle η_max 和 K_eff 的准自然实验。关键发现： 即使在控制 η_max 方差后，K_eff 仍然是次要驱动因素（2:1 而非 1:1 或 K_eff 主导）。 论文可表述为：\\\"当 capability 差异被控制时，diversity 浮现为统计上可检测的次要因素——但在 自然 panel 组合中，capability 差异（通过 η_max）压倒性地主导脆弱性。\\\"这强化了 robustness-first 设计建议：先筛选 capability，再在筛选后的池中考虑 diversity。\\n\\n在同一 capability tier 内，η_max 方差降低约 65-70%（因为同 tier 模型能力接近），而 K_eff 方差保持（同 tier 模型仍来自不同 families/architectures）。η_max 和 K_eff 的 confound 从 r=0.70（全池）降至 r≈0.35（tier 内），解开了回归中的多重共线性。在此条件下，K_eff 的边际信号——通常被 η_max 的强效应淹没——变得可检测。OLS 下 5/12 显著；clustered SE 后 保留 2/12，表明 K_eff 有微弱但真实的独立效应。主导比从 5:1 降至 2:1，但 η_max 仍然 主导。这支持论文叙事：K_eff 有方向性关联但在全池分析中被 η_max 压倒——当人为控制 η_max 方差时 K_eff 才浮现，这恰恰说明在自然变异条件下 η_max 是主要驱动因素。此外，within-tier R² 均值仅 0.18，说明 tier 内的面板脆弱性预测力大幅下降——进一步证明 η_max 的跨 tier 方差是预测力的主要来源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Two-Stage Panel Design Algorithm Benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 robustness-first 两阶段算法（filter η > threshold → maximize K_eff），对标 5 个 baseline 策略\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baselines\": [\n        \"random\",\n        \"max_keff\",\n        \"max_disagreement\",\n        \"strongest_k\",\n        \"uniform_family\"\n      ],\n      \"conditions\": 12,\n      \"min_eta_max_wins\": \"12/12\",\n      \"two_stage_vs_min_eta_max_improvement_pp\": [\n        0.3,\n        1.8\n      ],\n      \"two_stage_vs_min_eta_max_mean_improvement_pp\": 0.7,\n      \"two_stage_wins_vs_min_eta_max\": \"7/12\",\n      \"strategy_ranking\": {\n        \"rank_1\": \"two-stage (robustness-first + K_eff)\",\n        \"rank_2\": \"min_eta_max (robustness-first only)\",\n        \"rank_3\": \"strongest_k\",\n        \"rank_4\": \"uniform_family\",\n        \"rank_5\": \"max_disagreement\",\n        \"rank_6\": \"max_keff\",\n        \"rank_7\": \"random\"\n      },\n      \"max_keff_vs_random\": \"worse in 8/12 (includes weak models)\",\n      \"strongest_k_gap_from_min_eta_max\": \"1.2pp mean\",\n      \"asr_advantage_range\": [\n        0.038,\n        0.511\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Strategy Comparison (Mean ASR across 12 conditions)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"Mean ASR\",\n          \"Rank\",\n          \"Δ vs random (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"two-stage\",\n            \"0.112\",\n            \"1\",\n            \"-8.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"min_eta_max\",\n            \"0.119\",\n            \"2\",\n            \"-7.6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"strongest_k\",\n            \"0.131\",\n            \"3\",\n            \"-6.4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"uniform_family\",\n            \"0.158\",\n            \"4\",\n            \"-3.7\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"max_disagreement\",\n            \"0.172\",\n            \"5\",\n            \"-2.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random\",\n            \"0.195\",\n            \"6\",\n            \"0.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"max_keff\",\n            \"0.208\",\n            \"7\",\n            \"+1.3\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Two-Stage vs min_eta_max Per-Attack-Type\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Attack category\",\n          \"Conditions\",\n          \"Two-stage better?\",\n          \"Mean Δ (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Targeted\",\n            \"6\",\n            \"5/6\",\n            \"-1.1\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Shared-bias\",\n            \"6\",\n            \"2/6\",\n            \"-0.3\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Two-stage 算法的边际改进（0.7pp）虽然在统计上一致但实际影响不大——论文应诚实呈现这一点。 核心 practical recommendation 保持不变：robustness-first screening 是关键步骤，K_eff 优化是可选的次要步骤。max_keff 策略的失败（差于 random）是论文叙事的有力支撑——直观的 \\\"多样化 panel\\\" 建议在实践中适得其反。\\n\\nmin_eta_max 策略赢 12/12 因为 η_max 是主导脆弱性驱动因素。两阶段策略在 min_eta_max 基础上提供边际改进（mean 0.7pp）：在已通过 robustness 筛选的 judge 子集中，K_eff 的微弱次要效应（在 capability-matched 设置中可检测，如 plan_004 所示）被利用。改进最大 的条件是 targeted attacks（K_eff 方向为正 = diversity 有害 → 在 robustness-screened 池中最小化 K_eff 有帮助）。改进最小的条件是 shared-bias attacks（K_eff 方向为负 → diversity 在这些条件下是保护性的 → 最大化 K_eff 更优）。max_keff 策略表现差于 random 因为最大化 diversity 必然引入弱模型（r=0.70 tradeoff），直接提高了 η_max。 strongest_k 与 min_eta_max 差距仅 1.2pp——因为最强模型通常也最鲁棒，但 min_eta_max 是直接优化目标函数而 strongest_k 是代理指标。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-Judge ASR Concentration Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"计算每个 panel × attack 的 per-judge ASR 分布的 Gini 系数和 Shannon 熵，量化 adaptive adversary 是否针对特定 judge\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"panels\": 455,\n      \"conditions\": 12,\n      \"gini_targeted_mean\": 0.78,\n      \"gini_targeted_range\": [\n        0.72,\n        0.85\n      ],\n      \"gini_shared_bias_mean\": 0.43,\n      \"gini_shared_bias_range\": [\n        0.35,\n        0.52\n      ],\n      \"gini_targeted_vs_shared_mannwhitney_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"entropy_targeted_mean\": 0.82,\n      \"entropy_shared_bias_mean\": 1.45,\n      \"gini_eta_max_correlation\": 0.83,\n      \"top1_judge_asr_fraction_targeted\": 0.61,\n      \"top1_judge_asr_fraction_shared\": 0.38\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"ASR Concentration by Attack Category\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Attack Type\",\n          \"Category\",\n          \"Gini (mean)\",\n          \"Entropy (mean)\",\n          \"Top-1 judge ASR fraction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"prompt_injection\",\n            \"targeted\",\n            \"0.82\",\n            \"0.73\",\n            \"0.65\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"score_manipulation\",\n            \"targeted\",\n            \"0.79\",\n            \"0.78\",\n            \"0.62\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"position_bias\",\n            \"targeted\",\n            \"0.74\",\n            \"0.94\",\n            \"0.56\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"sycophancy\",\n            \"shared-bias\",\n            \"0.45\",\n            \"1.38\",\n            \"0.40\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"verbosity_bias\",\n            \"shared-bias\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"1.47\",\n            \"0.37\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"authority_bias\",\n            \"shared-bias\",\n            \"0.41\",\n            \"1.50\",\n            \"0.36\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ASR 浓度分析为 η_max 主导性提供了微观机制证据，超越了回归系数的间接推断。审稿人常问 \\\"what's the mechanism?\\\"——本实验直接回答：targeted adversary 将攻击集中在 weakest judge 上（Gini>0.7），使 η_max 成为 panel 脆弱性的充分统计量。shared-bias 下 ASR 更分散 解释了为什么 K_eff 在这类攻击中为负——diversity 提供 partial immunity 因为并非所有 judges 都同样受 shared bias 影响。此发现独立验证 GAM taxonomy。\\n\\nTargeted attacks（prompt injection, score manipulation, position bias）利用特定 judge 的个体弱点——adversary 的攻击策略集中在 panel 中最脆弱的 judge 上。这导致 ASR 分布 高度集中（Gini 0.72-0.85）：top-1 judge 贡献了约 61% 的 panel 总 ASR。这是 η_max 主导性的直接微观机制证据——vulnerability 确实集中在 weakest link。相比之下，shared-bias attacks（sycophancy, verbosity, authority）利用多个 judges 共享的认知偏差，ASR 更 均匀地分布在 panel 成员间（Gini 0.35-0.52），top-1 judge 仅贡献约 38%。Gini 与 η_max 的高相关（r=0.83）直接证明 panel-level vulnerability 与 judge-level concentration 是同一现象的两个面。这为 GAM 6:6 split 提供了独立的 mechanistic 验证——targeted 和 shared-bias 不仅在 K_eff 方向上分裂，在 ASR concentration 模式上也完全分裂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Diversity-Capability Tradeoff Visualization\",\n    \"description\": \"绘制 K_eff vs η_max scatter，拟合 tradeoff curve，计算 Pareto frontier，按 tier 分层\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_keff_etamax_r\": 0.7,\n      \"overall_keff_etamax_r_ci95\": [\n        0.66,\n        0.74\n      ],\n      \"tier_stratified\": {\n        \"base_tier_r\": 0.52,\n        \"mid_tier_r\": 0.48,\n        \"frontier_tier_r\": 0.35\n      },\n      \"pareto_frontier_size\": 12,\n      \"pareto_dominance_pct\": \"97.4% of panels dominated\",\n      \"pareto_frontier_composition\": \"predominantly low-K_eff, low-η_max panels\",\n      \"tradeoff_curve_fit\": \"monotone increasing, concave\",\n      \"within_family_r\": 0.81,\n      \"cross_family_r\": 0.65\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Tradeoff Correlation by Stratification\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Stratification\",\n          \"N panels\",\n          \"r(K_eff, η_max)\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Full pool\",\n            \"455\",\n            \"0.70\",\n            \"[0.66, 0.74]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Base tier only\",\n            \"84\",\n            \"0.52\",\n            \"[0.38, 0.64]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Within-family\",\n            \"varies\",\n            \"0.81\",\n            \"[0.73, 0.87]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cross-family\",\n            \"varies\",\n            \"0.65\",\n            \"[0.58, 0.71]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"可视化使 structural constraint 具象化——审稿人直观理解为什么 max_keff 策略失败（右上角） 而 min_eta_max 策略成功（左下角）。Tier 内相关降低的发现为 two-stage algorithm 提供了 理论基础：capability screening 打破了跨 tier 的 strong tradeoff，使后续 diversity 优化在弱 tradeoff 条件下进行。此 figure 应作为论文 Fig 3 或 Fig 4。\\n\\nr=0.70 的 structural correlation 源于当前 LLM 生态系统的特性：最大化 K_eff 需要包含来自 不同 capability tiers 的模型（不同 family × tier 组合提供最大 behavioral diversity）， 这必然引入能力较弱的 judges，推高 η_max。Tier 分层后 r 降低（base: 0.52, frontier: 0.35） 说明 tradeoff 在 tier 内较弱——within tier 的 diversity（来自不同 architecture/training） 不需要大幅牺牲 capability。这支持 two-stage recommendation 的逻辑：先筛选 capability tier（打破跨 tier tradeoff），再在 tier 内最大化 diversity（利用弱化的 within-tier tradeoff）。 Pareto frontier 几乎全部由 low-K_eff, low-η_max panels 占据——no free lunch，但 robustness-first selection 自然落在 Pareto frontier 上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Panel Size Sensitivity Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"测试 K=3,5,7,9 不同 panel 尺寸下 η_max 主导性是否持续\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"panel_sizes\": [\n        3,\n        5,\n        7,\n        9\n      ],\n      \"panels_per_size\": [\n        455,\n        3003,\n        6435,\n        5005\n      ],\n      \"eta_max_sig_by_k_clustered_se\": {\n        \"k3\": \"8/12\",\n        \"k5\": \"9/12\",\n        \"k7\": \"9/12\",\n        \"k9\": \"8/12\"\n      },\n      \"keff_sig_by_k_clustered_se\": {\n        \"k3\": \"0/12\",\n        \"k5\": \"1/12\",\n        \"k7\": \"1/12\",\n        \"k9\": \"2/12\"\n      },\n      \"dominance_ratio_by_k\": {\n        \"k3\": \"8:0\",\n        \"k5\": \"9:1\",\n        \"k7\": \"9:1\",\n        \"k9\": \"4:1\"\n      },\n      \"eta_max_effect_size_trend\": \"decreasing with K (from 0.42 at K=3 to 0.31 at K=9)\",\n      \"keff_effect_size_trend\": \"stable (0.12-0.16 across all K)\",\n      \"min_eta_max_wins_by_k\": {\n        \"k3\": \"12/12\",\n        \"k5\": \"12/12\",\n        \"k7\": \"12/12\",\n        \"k9\": \"12/12\"\n      },\n      \"se_inflation_by_k\": [\n        2.5,\n        4.1,\n        6.3,\n        7.8\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Panel Size Sensitivity Summary (Clustered SE)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"Panels\",\n          \"η_max sig\",\n          \"K_eff sig\",\n          \"Ratio\",\n          \"SE inflation\",\n          \"η_max β (mean)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"3\",\n            \"455\",\n            \"8/12\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"8:0\",\n            \"2.5x\",\n            \"0.42\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5\",\n            \"3003\",\n            \"9/12\",\n            \"1/12\",\n            \"9:1\",\n            \"4.1x\",\n            \"0.38\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"7\",\n            \"6435\",\n            \"9/12\",\n            \"1/12\",\n            \"9:1\",\n            \"6.3x\",\n            \"0.34\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"9\",\n            \"5005\",\n            \"8/12\",\n            \"2/12\",\n            \"4:1\",\n            \"7.8x\",\n            \"0.31\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Panel size sensitivity 提供两个关键发现：(1) η_max 主导性在 K=3 到 K=9 范围内稳定持续， 确认 weakest-link 不是小 panel 的 artifact；(2) SE 膨胀随 K 急剧增加，为方法论 contribution（non-independence correction 的必要性）提供量化支撑。K=9 时 K_eff 达到 2/12 显著但 effect size 仍微小——power 增加检测到了真实但 practically insignificant 的效应。论文 supplementary 中可报告此分析作为 robustness check。\\n\\nη_max 主导性在所有 K 下持续因为 weakest-link 机制是 scale-invariant：无论 panel 有多少 judges，adversary 总是针对最脆弱的那个。K 增加时 η_max 的 effect size 略降（0.42→0.31） 因为更大 panel 中 majority vote 的容错能力增加——单个 judge 的失败更难翻转整个 panel。 但 η_max 仍然主导，因为 adversary 不只针对一个 judge——adaptive adversary 可以同时攻击 多个弱 judges。K_eff 在 K=9 时达到 2/12 显著：更多 panels（5005）提供了更多统计 power， 但 effect size 保持微小（0.12-0.16）。SE 膨胀随 K 急剧增加（每个 model 出现在更多 panels 中），从 K=3 的 2.5x 到 K=9 的 7.8x。这为 non-independence 校正方法的必要性 提供了更强的论据——在 K=7 或 K=9 下使用 OLS 会产生极度膨胀的显著性计数。 min_eta_max 策略在所有 K 下赢 12/12，确认 practical recommendation 对 panel size 鲁棒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"VIF + Multicollinearity Diagnostic\",\n    \"description\": \"计算 VIF、partial correlations、residualized K_eff regression，应用 Bonferroni/FDR 校正，尝试 beta regression\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpu_needed\": false,\n      \"raw_vif_keff\": 2.96,\n      \"raw_vif_eta_max\": 2.96,\n      \"residualized_vif_keff\": 1.0,\n      \"partial_correlation_keff_asr_given_eta\": 0.18,\n      \"partial_correlation_eta_asr_given_keff\": 0.42,\n      \"bonferroni_eta_max_sig\": \"7/12\",\n      \"bonferroni_keff_sig\": \"2/12\",\n      \"fdr_eta_max_sig\": \"8/12\",\n      \"fdr_keff_sig\": \"3/12\",\n      \"beta_regression_eta_max_sig\": \"10/12\",\n      \"beta_regression_keff_sig\": \"4/12 (3+/1-)\",\n      \"beta_regression_dispersion_phi\": [\n        3.2,\n        8.7\n      ],\n      \"condition_number\": 4.8,\n      \"reviewer_blocking_issue\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Multicollinearity Diagnostics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\",\n          \"Threshold\",\n          \"Status\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"VIF (K_eff, raw)\",\n            \"2.96\",\n            \"< 5 (strict) / < 10 (standard)\",\n            \"PASS\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VIF (K_eff, residualized)\",\n            \"1.00\",\n            \"< 5\",\n            \"PASS\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Condition number\",\n            \"4.8\",\n            \"< 30\",\n            \"PASS\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Partial r(K_eff, ASR | η_max)\",\n            \"0.18\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"Weak\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Partial r(η_max, ASR | K_eff)\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"Moderate-strong\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Method Comparison with Multiple Testing Correction\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"η_max sig\",\n          \"K_eff sig\",\n          \"K_eff direction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"OLS + FDR\",\n            \"11/12\",\n            \"8/12\",\n            \"7+/1-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OLS + Bonferroni\",\n            \"7/12\",\n            \"2/12\",\n            \"2+/0-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Clustered SE + FDR\",\n            \"8/12\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Beta regression + FDR\",\n            \"10/12\",\n            \"4/12\",\n            \"3+/1-\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"VIF 分析消除了审稿人 RC1 的 last-resort 攻击角度——multicollinearity is moderate, not pathological。r=0.70 在经验社会科学中常见（e.g., income and education）， standard practice 是报告 VIF 并继续。Beta regression 提供了 distributional robustness check：结论与 log-log OLS 一致。论文可在 methods 节用一段话报告 VIF diagnostics 并在 supplementary 中给出完整表格。\\n\\nRaw VIF ≈ 2.96 直接由 r=0.70 的 confound 决定（VIF = 1/(1-r²) = 1/(1-0.49) = 1.96 在 bivariate 情况下；加上 tier indicators 后升至约 2.96）。VIF < 5 远低于标准 reviewer concern 阈值（通常 VIF > 10），甚至低于 stricter 标准（VIF > 5）。Residualization 后 VIF 降至 1.0（by construction），residualized K_eff 的 partial correlation 仅 0.18 vs η_max 的 0.42——直接量化了主导性差异。Beta regression 作为 ASR ∈ [0,1] 的 distributional 替代方案：η_max 显著性从 log-log OLS 的 11/12 降至 10/12（beta regression 对极端值更鲁棒），K_eff 从 8/12 升至 4/12（beta regression 更好地处理 heteroscedasticity）。Condition number 4.8 < 30 确认无有害多重共线性。Bonferroni 校正（most conservative）给出 η_max 7/12 vs K_eff 2/12——即使在最保守的多重比较 校正下 η_max 仍显著主导。无 reviewer-blocking issue。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Aggregation Gradient Under Clustered SE\",\n    \"description\": \"在 clustered SE 和 bootstrap 下重新运行 4 种聚合规则 + 新增 veto rule，验证聚合梯度是否为真实效应而非 overlap 伪迹\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"aggregation_rules\": [\n        \"majority\",\n        \"weighted\",\n        \"threshold\",\n        \"bayesian\",\n        \"veto\"\n      ],\n      \"correction_methods\": [\n        \"OLS\",\n        \"clustered_se\",\n        \"bootstrap_v2\"\n      ],\n      \"majority_clustered_se\": {\n        \"eta_sig\": \"8/12\",\n        \"keff_sig\": \"0/12\"\n      },\n      \"weighted_clustered_se\": {\n        \"eta_sig\": \"6/12\",\n        \"keff_sig\": \"1/12\",\n        \"keff_direction\": \"1+\"\n      },\n      \"threshold_clustered_se\": {\n        \"eta_sig\": \"10/12\",\n        \"keff_sig\": \"4/12\",\n        \"keff_direction\": \"3+/1-\",\n        \"r2\": 0.87\n      },\n      \"bayesian_clustered_se\": {\n        \"eta_sig\": \"5/12\",\n        \"keff_sig\": \"4/12\",\n        \"keff_direction\": \"1+/3-\",\n        \"keff_negative_frac\": \"3/4\"\n      },\n      \"veto_clustered_se\": {\n        \"eta_sig\": \"11/12\",\n        \"keff_sig\": \"0/12\",\n        \"r2\": 0.82\n      },\n      \"bayesian_bootstrap\": {\n        \"eta_sig\": \"3/12\",\n        \"keff_sig\": \"3/12\",\n        \"keff_direction\": \"0+/3-\",\n        \"keff_negative_frac\": \"3/3\"\n      },\n      \"gradient_preserved_under_correction\": true,\n      \"bayesian_keff_flip_genuine\": true,\n      \"aggregation_gradient_order\": \"veto > threshold > majority > weighted > bayesian\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Aggregation Gradient Under Clustered SE\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Rule\",\n          \"η_max sig\",\n          \"K_eff sig\",\n          \"K_eff neg frac\",\n          \"R²\",\n          \"Gradient position\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Veto\",\n            \"11/12\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"0.82\",\n            \"Maximum vulnerability\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Threshold\",\n            \"10/12\",\n            \"4/12\",\n            \"1/4\",\n            \"0.87\",\n            \"High\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Majority\",\n            \"8/12\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"0.28\",\n            \"Moderate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Weighted\",\n            \"6/12\",\n            \"1/12\",\n            \"0/1\",\n            \"0.26\",\n            \"Low-moderate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Bayesian\",\n            \"5/12\",\n            \"4/12\",\n            \"3/4\",\n            \"0.09\",\n            \"Minimum vulnerability\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Bayesian K_eff Direction Detail\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Correction\",\n          \"K_eff sig total\",\n          \"K_eff positive\",\n          \"K_eff negative\",\n          \"Neg fraction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"OLS\",\n            \"7/12\",\n            \"1\",\n            \"6\",\n            \"6/7 (86%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Clustered SE\",\n            \"4/12\",\n            \"1\",\n            \"3\",\n            \"3/4 (75%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Bootstrap v2\",\n            \"3/12\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"3\",\n            \"3/3 (100%)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"聚合梯度在校正下的稳健性是论文的独立贡献——它不受 non-independence concern 的影响，因为 它描述的是投票规则数学的 structural 性质。Veto rule 的加入使梯度两端更 extreme： veto（pure weakest-link）vs Bayesian（weakest-link neutralized + diversity flip）。 论文可以将此呈现为 defense design spectrum——practitioners 根据其对 false positive vs false negative 的偏好选择适当位置。Bayesian K_eff 在 bootstrap 下 3/3 negative 是 cleanest possible evidence for the flip。\\n\\n聚合梯度在 clustered SE 下保持，因为不同投票规则产生的脆弱性差异是 structural/mathematical 的，不是 panel overlap 的伪迹。Threshold（unanimity）要求所有 judges 一致，使单个 judge 的 failure 直接传导为 panel failure——R²=0.87 说明 panel 结构几乎完全决定了 threshold voting 下的脆弱性。这种强 structural 效应在 clustered SE 下大量存活（η_max 10/12, K_eff 4/12）。Veto rule（单个 judge 可否决）是 weakest-link 的极端化——η_max 几乎 完美预测（11/12），K_eff 被完全压倒（0/12）。 Bayesian calibration 翻转 K_eff 方向的关键机制：Bayesian 使用 prior accuracy 下调不可靠 judges 的权重，有效中和了 weakest-link 通道。η_max 的直接效应被削弱（11→5/12）。 剩余的 K_eff 信号主要来自 shared-bias 条件（diversity 保护性的部分），因此净方向为负。 在 bootstrap 下，Bayesian K_eff 仅 3/12 显著但全部为负（3/3 negative fraction）—— direction flip 是真实的。这确认 aggregation 是独立于 non-independence correction 的 control lever。论文的 prescriptive conclusion（robustness-first + Bayesian = dual-channel defense）在最严格校正下依然成立。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Open-Ended Generation Benchmark Extension\",\n    \"description\": \"在 MT-Bench 风格的 open-ended generation 任务上测试 weakest-link 假说，超越 MCQ 格式\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"benchmark\": \"MT-Bench (8 categories)\",\n      \"judge_format\": \"1-10 scale scoring\",\n      \"models_available\": 12,\n      \"panels\": 220,\n      \"attack_types\": [\n        \"style_manipulation\",\n        \"length_inflation\",\n        \"format_gaming\"\n      ],\n      \"conditions\": 6,\n      \"eta_max_sig_ols\": \"5/6\",\n      \"keff_sig_ols\": \"3/6 (2+/1-)\",\n      \"eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"4/6\",\n      \"keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/6\",\n      \"r2_mean\": 0.22,\n      \"gam_generation_split\": {\n        \"style_manipulation\": \"shared-bias (negative K_eff)\",\n        \"length_inflation\": \"shared-bias (negative K_eff)\",\n        \"format_gaming\": \"targeted (positive K_eff)\"\n      },\n      \"min_eta_max_wins\": \"6/6\",\n      \"cross_format_consistency\": \"η_max dominant in both MCQ and generation\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Generation Benchmark Results (Clustered SE)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"η_max sig?\",\n          \"K_eff sig?\",\n          \"K_eff GAM dir\",\n          \"R²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"style_manipulation × MT-Bench\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"negative\",\n            \"0.19\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"length_inflation × MT-Bench\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"negative\",\n            \"0.24\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"format_gaming × MT-Bench\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"positive\",\n            \"0.23\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-Format Consistency\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Format\",\n          \"η_max sig (CL-SE)\",\n          \"K_eff sig (CL-SE)\",\n          \"Dominance ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MCQ (MMLU+ARC)\",\n            \"8/12\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"8:0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Generation (MT-Bench)\",\n            \"4/6\",\n            \"0/6\",\n            \"4:0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Combined\",\n            \"12/18\",\n            \"0/18\",\n            \"12:0\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Generation extension 消除了\\\"MCQ-specific artifact\\\"的审稿人质疑。η_max 主导性跨 task format 通用性是论文 generalizability 论证的关键证据。R² 降低反映了 generation evaluation 的内在 noise，但 relative driver importance（η_max >> K_eff）完全保持。 此实验可作为 Section 5 的扩展分析或 supplementary material。\\n\\nη_max 主导性在 generation 任务中持续因为底层机制相同：无论 judges 评估 MCQ 正确性还是 generation 质量，adversary 都针对最可操纵的 judge。Generation 的 1-10 scale 提供了比 MCQ binary 更多的操纵空间（微妙的 style/format manipulation 可以影响 rubric-based scoring），但 vulnerability 的 distribution across judges 仍然是高度不均匀的—— 某些 judges 对 length inflation 或 format gaming 特别敏感。R² 较低（0.22 vs MCQ 的 0.30）因为 generation evaluation 有更多 idiosyncratic variance（rubric interpretation, 文化偏好等）。K_eff 在 OLS 下 3/6 显著但 clustered SE 后归零——与 MCQ 完全一致。 GAM 分类中，style manipulation 和 length inflation 属于 shared-bias（所有 LLM judges 都倾向于给更长/更 polished 的回答更高分），而 format gaming 属于 targeted（利用特定 model 的 format parsing 差异）。12 模型（部分 API 模型不支持 generation evaluation） 给出 220 panels，足够进行 regression analysis。min_eta_max 策略在 generation 上同样 赢 6/6，确认 practical recommendation 跨 task format 通用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Partial-Knowledge Adversary Model\",\n    \"description\": \"模拟 adversary 仅知道 judge family labels（不知具体脆弱性 profile）的 realistic threat model\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"knowledge_levels\": [\n        \"full (baseline)\",\n        \"family-only\",\n        \"random\"\n      ],\n      \"asr_reduction_family_vs_full_pct\": 18,\n      \"asr_reduction_random_vs_full_pct\": 42,\n      \"family_knowledge_eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"7/12\",\n      \"family_knowledge_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/12\",\n      \"family_knowledge_dominance_ratio\": \"7:0\",\n      \"random_targeting_eta_max_sig_clustered_se\": \"3/12\",\n      \"random_targeting_keff_sig_clustered_se\": \"0/12\",\n      \"family_knowledge_r2_mean\": 0.24,\n      \"family_label_attack_efficiency\": 0.82\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Adversary Knowledge Level Comparison (Clustered SE)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Knowledge level\",\n          \"Mean ASR\",\n          \"ASR vs full (%)\",\n          \"η_max sig\",\n          \"K_eff sig\",\n          \"R²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Full knowledge\",\n            \"0.195\",\n            \"100%\",\n            \"8/12\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"0.30\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Family-only\",\n            \"0.160\",\n            \"82%\",\n            \"7/12\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"0.24\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random\",\n            \"0.113\",\n            \"58%\",\n            \"3/12\",\n            \"0/12\",\n            \"0.08\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Family Label Informativeness\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Attack efficiency (family/full)\",\n            \"0.82\",\n            \"Family labels highly informative for targeting\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Family-vulnerability correlation\",\n            \"0.61\",\n            \"Moderate; same family shares weaknesses\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"η_max sig retention (family vs full)\",\n            \"7/8\",\n            \"Targeting still exploits weakest link\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Partial-knowledge 实验将论文结论从 worst-case（omniscient adversary）扩展至 realistic threat model。Family-only adversary 保留 82% 攻击效率这一发现对 practical defense implications 至关重要——defenders 不能依赖\\\"adversary 不知道 panel 具体组成\\\"的假设， 因为 family-level knowledge 几乎 sufficient。η_max 在所有 knowledge levels 下主导， K_eff 在所有 knowledge levels 下为 0/12——核心发现对 adversary 能力假设鲁棒。 Random targeting 的 R²=0.08 呼应 plan_003 的 RF 结论：panel 结构的预测力依赖于 adversary 的 strategic targeting——这是论文 adaptive vs random 对比叙事的第三个 independent evidence line。\\n\\nFamily-only adversary 的 ASR 仅降 18%（而非 random 的 42%），因为 family labels 与 vulnerability profiles 有中等相关：同 family 模型共享 training pipeline 和 architectural biases，adversary 可基于 family 推断出 approximately correct 的攻击 策略。η_max 仍然主导（7/12 vs full-knowledge 的 8/12）因为 family-level targeting 仍 preferentially hits weaker judges——family labels 虽然 noisy 但 informationally above chance。K_eff 在 partial-knowledge 下同样为 0/12——diversity 在任何 knowledge level 下都不是 independent protective factor after correction。Attack efficiency 0.82 意味着 family labels 提供了 82% of full-knowledge targeting effectiveness——这对 ecological validity 至关重要：现实中 adversary 通常知道 panel 的 model families （从 API endpoint, response style 等推断），因此 full-knowledge 结果的 relevance 不仅限于理论上限。Random targeting 下 η_max 仅 3/12 显著——random adversary 无法有效 利用 individual weaknesses，说明 η_max 的 predictive power 依赖于 adversary 的 targeting ability，与 adaptive vs RF contrast（plan_003）形成完整呼应。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1174,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1174}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019dgPcNQNJV5xmQBQ4oYXTH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015nSFZiXGXLphzt6wAdh18E","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/cert_manip_resist_eval/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T221131/best/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12280,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12280},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca7c92ca-7226-4597-b435-bb7be4a94344","uuid":"1956cccd-23a7-42e2-8e7e-6dc7ebb5396f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015nSFZiXGXLphzt6wAdh18E","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — cert_manip_resist_eval (v5: Post-Clustered-SE Reframe, D019)\n2\t\n3\t> Last updated: 2026-05-22 | Reason: Bootstrap v2 (Reviewer-verified): η_max 5-11/12 (bootstrap 5/12 most reliable), K_eff 0-1/12. η_max:K_eff ratio 5:1 confirms dominance. GAM 6:6 split confirmed. Aggregation gradient independent.\n4\t\n5\t## Target\n6\tEMNLP 2026 (via ARR)\n7\t\n8\t## Title Candidates\n9\t1. \"The Weakest Judge Wins: What Really Drives LLM Evaluation Panel Vulnerability Under Adversarial Attack\"\n10\t2. \"Weakest Link, Not Diversity: Adversarial Vulnerability in Multi-Judge LLM Evaluation\"\n11\t3. \"The Diversity Trap: Why Adding More Judges Doesn't Make LLM Evaluation Safer\" (softened with honest reporting)\n12\t\n13\t## Core Insight\n14\tMulti-judge LLM evaluation panels are widely assumed to benefit from judge diversity. We conduct the first large-scale empirical study (15 models, 455 panels, 6 attacks, 2 benchmarks) decomposing panel vulnerability into individual weakness (η_max) and structural diversity (K_eff). Key findings: (1) **η_max dominates** panel vulnerability (5-11/12 conditions significant depending on correction method; wild cluster bootstrap — the most reliable method for small cluster counts — gives 5/12, with η_max:K_eff ratio of 5:1); (2) K_eff shows **directional but statistically fragile** association with vulnerability — point estimates predominantly positive (diversity increases risk), but significance collapses from 8/12 (OLS) to 0-1/12 after non-independence correction (bootstrap 1/12, clustered SE 0/12); (3) **GAM reveals a clean attack-type split**: K_eff is positive (harmful) for targeted attacks and negative (protective) for shared-bias attacks — a 6:6 pattern masked by linear regression; (4) **Aggregation rule choice fundamentally modulates vulnerability**: Bayesian calibration reverses K_eff direction (6/7 negative) and weakens η_max (9/12), while threshold voting amplifies both (R²=0.89).\n15\t\n16\t## Hook\n17\t\"Panel security against adversarial manipulation is dominated by the weakest individual judge — not panel diversity. But how you aggregate judges' votes determines whether diversity becomes a vulnerability or a defense.\"\n18\t\n19\t## Novelty Positioning\n20\tWe do NOT claim diversity is harmful with high statistical confidence — K_eff's independent effect is directional but fragile under rigorous correction. Our contributions are:\n21\t1. **First large-scale empirical decomposition** of panel vulnerability into η_max and K_eff in the LLM-judge domain (15 models, 455 panels), with transparent robustness analysis showing η_max dominates (5:1 over K_eff under bootstrap inference)\n22\t2. **Attack-type taxonomy with clean mechanistic split**: GAM reveals K_eff positive for targeted attacks, negative for shared-bias attacks (6:6 split), explaining WHEN diversity helps vs hurts\n23\t3. **Aggregation as a control lever**: voting rule modulates the diversity-vulnerability relationship — Bayesian reverses K_eff direction, threshold amplifies it (D017, independent of non-independence concern)\n24\t4. **Robustness-first panel design**: min(η_max) strategy wins 12/12 conditions (Claim 6, unaffected by SE correction)\n25\t5. **Structural barriers**: diversity-capability tradeoff (r=0.70), family label unreliability (confirmed at 15-model)\n26\t6. **Alternative diversity metrics robustness**: η_max dominance holds across operationalizations — Q-stat only 2/12 sig (r=0.674 with K_eff), disagreement 8/12, κ-diversity 7/12. K_eff practical effect size: IQR → Δ ASR = 1.3pp (directional but practically small)\n27\t7. **Methodological transparency**: explicit reporting of how significance changes across OLS → clustered SE → mixed effects, demonstrating the importance of accounting for panel overlap in combinatorial evaluation designs\n28\t\n29\t## Core Claims\n30\t\n31\t### Claim 1 (Primary): Weakest-Link Dominance\n32\t**Statement**: Under adaptive adversarial attacks, panel vulnerability is **dominated by individual judge weakness (η_max)**. η_max remains significant in 5-8/12 conditions after non-independence correction (wild bootstrap 5/12, clustered SE 8/12, mixed effects 7/12). K_eff (diversity) shows directional association but significance is fragile (bootstrap 1/12, clustered SE 0/12). The η_max:K_eff dominance ratio is 5:1 under bootstrap — stronger than OLS's 11:8 ≈ 1.4:1.\n33\t**Evidence** (15-model, 455 panels, 12 conditions, D019+D021):\n34\t- **Regression spec**: log-log OLS: log(ASR + ε) ~ const + log(K_eff) + log(η_max + ε)\n35\t- **Standard OLS**: η_max **11/12**, K_eff **8/12** (7+/1−) — inflated by panel non-independence\n36\t- **Wild cluster bootstrap v2** (Reviewer-verified, B=9999, Rademacher, 3-position max-p): η_max **5/12**, K_eff **1/12** (mmlu×PI only) — conservative lower bound. Per-position analysis: position 0 gives 6/12 (cluster imbalance: claude-3-haiku=91 panels vs qwen2.5-14b=1), positions 1&2 each give **9/12** (more balanced clusters, consistent with clustered SE). Max-across-positions is legitimate conservative bound but tightened by position 0 imbalance.\n37\t- **Clustered SE** (15 judge clusters, CR1): η_max **8/12**, K_eff **0/12** — consistent with per-position bootstrap 1&2\n38\t- **Mixed effects** (random judge intercepts): η_max **7/12**, K_eff **3/12** (mmlu×PI, arc×PI, arc×PB)\n39\t- SE inflation ~2.5x (consistent with 91/455 panel overlap)\n40\t- Bootstrap η_max shows benchmark asymmetry: MMLU 4/6, ARC 1/6 survive. Likely cause: MMLU 4-choice format provides more scoring variance than ARC 2-choice, giving η_max more signal. arc×PI η_max completely lost (OLS p=3e-14 → bootstrap all NS) — signal was entirely from panel overlap.\n41\t- **arc×sycophancy exception**: No longer significant under any correction (OLS p=0.013 → bootstrap 0.06 → clustered 0.441 → mixed 0.136). Reported as directional observation, not robust claim.\n42\t- **Alternative diversity metrics (OLS)**: Q-stat 2/12, disagreement 8/12 (7+/1−), κ-diversity 7/12 (7+/0−). Q-stat (lowest correlation with K_eff, r=0.674) gives lowest diversity significance — further supports η_max as dominant driver regardless of diversity operationalization.\n43\t- **Practical effect size**: K_eff IQR change → Δ ASR = 1.3pp (clustered SE CIs contain zero in 11/12 conditions). Even under OLS, diversity effect is practically small.\n44\t**Strength**: η_max dominant (5:1 ratio over K_eff under bootstrap). Absolute significance lower than OLS (5/12 vs 11/12) but relative dominance stronger. K_eff directional but fragile and practically small.\n45\t**Headline**: \"η_max dominates panel vulnerability (5:1 over K_eff); both channels inflated by panel non-independence, but η_max survives correction while K_eff does not.\"\n46\t\n47\t### Claim 1b (Secondary): Attack-Type Taxonomy — GAM 6:6 Split\n48\t**Statement**: GAM analysis reveals that K_eff's direction cleanly splits by attack mechanism: **positive (diversity harmful) for targeted attacks** (prompt_injection, score_manipulation, position_bias × 2 benchmarks = 6 conditions) and **negative (diversity protective) for shared-bias attacks** (sycophancy, verbosity_bias, authority_bias × 2 benchmarks = 6 conditions). This 6:6 pattern is masked by linear OLS which shows 7+/1−/4NS.\n49\t**Evidence**: GAM partial effects, 455 panels, 12 conditions.\n50\t- Targeted attacks (exploit judge-specific weaknesses): K_eff partial effect positive in all 6 conditions\n51\t- Shared-bias attacks (exploit common cognitive biases): K_eff partial effect negative in all 6 conditions\n52\t- **Caveat**: GAM significance of individual conditions needs clustered SE / bootstrapped CI (pending); the structural pattern is the main finding, not individual p-values\n53\t**Strength**: Moderate-to-strong as qualitative taxonomic contribution. The clean 6:6 split provides mechanistic explanatory power beyond individual significance counts. Confirmed under correct 3/3/9 tier classification (GAM tier-fix rerun: all macro conclusions unchanged).\n54\t\n55\t### Claim 2 (Empirical): Predictability Gap — Panel Composition Explains RF But Not Adaptive Vulnerability\n56\t**Statement**: Panel composition (η_max + K_eff) explains substantially more variance under random faults (R²=0.73-0.81) than under adaptive attacks (lower R²). K_eff is positively associated with vulnerability in BOTH regimes, but: under RF, this association is genuine (survives all corrections, 2/2); under adaptive, it is largely artifactual (0-1/12 after correction). Adaptive adversaries introduce strategic variance beyond what panel structure can predict.\n57\t**Evidence** (15-model, 455 panels, D021+RF validation, Reviewer-verified):\n58\t- **Random-fault regime** (error = 1 - clean_accuracy, Monte Carlo 10000):\n59\t  - K_eff **positive** std_β = +0.215 (MMLU), +0.379 (ARC) — diversity associated with HIGHER error\n60\t  - K_eff significant **2/2** under ALL correction methods (OLS, clustered SE, bootstrap)\n61\t  - R² = 0.73-0.81 (highly predictable)\n62\t- **Adaptive regime** (D021):\n63\t  - K_eff also positive under OLS (7+/1−) but significance collapses to **0-1/12** after correction\n64\t  - R² substantially lower\n65\t- **Contrast**: NOT \"diversity helps under RF but hurts under adaptive\" — diversity is harmful in both. The contrast is: K_eff's harmful association is GENUINE under RF but INFLATED/ARTIFACTUAL under adaptive due to panel non-independence\n66\t- ΔR² gap: RF regime is highly predictable from panel composition; adaptive regime is not\n67\t**Correct interpretation**: Random faults are structurally determined by panel composition (hence high R² and genuine K_eff effect). Adaptive adversaries exploit weaknesses strategically, introducing variance that panel-level predictors cannot capture. K_eff in the adaptive regime appears significant under OLS only because of panel overlap inflation.\n68\t**Strength**: Strong as predictability gap (R² contrast). The finding that K_eff is genuine under RF but artifactual under adaptive is a clean methodological insight about when non-independence correction matters most.\n69\t\n70\t### Claim 3 (Empirical): Diversity-Capability Tradeoff\n71\t**Statement**: In the current LLM ecosystem, maximizing panel diversity (K_eff) structurally introduces less capable/robust models. The correlation r=+0.700 is a structural constraint — diversity and capability are partially opposed in the current model ecosystem.\n72\t**Evidence**:\n73\t- K_eff-η_max correlation: r = +0.700 (15-model)\n74\t- Under standard OLS: K_eff significant 8/12 (7+/1−) after residualizing η_max\n75\t- **D019 caveat**: Under clustered SE, K_eff drops to 0/12; mixed effects gives 3/12. The \"independent predictive effect\" of K_eff beyond η_max is directional but NOT statistically robust after correcting for non-independence. The structural correlation (r=0.700) itself is unaffected by SE correction — only the regression significance of K_eff as independent predictor changes.\n76\t**Framing**: The tradeoff is real as a structural constraint (r=0.700). Whether K_eff has an independent causal effect beyond η_max cannot be confidently established from this data — K_eff's significance is fragile under correction, and the high confound makes disentanglement unreliable.\n77\t**Strength**: Moderate (structural correlation strong; independent effect fragile). Causal language avoided.\n78\t\n79\t### Claim 4 (Methodological): Family Labels ≠ Diversity\n80\t**Statement**: Model family labels (Qwen/Llama/Mistral/Anthropic/OpenAI/Google) do not predict judge independence. Capability proximity is the primary driver of inter-judge correlation.\n81\t**Evidence**:\n82\t- 6-model: Mann-Whitney U p=0.206, permutation p=0.427\n83\t- **15-model (confirmed)**: p=0.179 (MMLU), p=0.385 (ARC). 14 within-family pairs, 91 cross-family pairs. Still not significant.\n84\t- Within-family MI variance is high (e.g., llama-70b↔8b MI only 0.05 due to capability gap > family similarity)\n85\t**Strength**: Moderate. Consistent across 6→15 model scaling.\n86\t\n87\t### ~~Claim 5 (Methodological): Gaussian Copula Failure~~ → DOWNGRADED to observation\n88\t**Original statement**: Gaussian copula systematically underestimates MI by 10-21×.\n89\t**15-model result**: MI_obs/MI_gaussian mean ratio = **0.93** (MMLU), **0.90** (ARC, robust). Copula fits well at 15-model scale. The 6-model 10-21× was a small-sample artifact (15 pairs → 105 pairs, extreme values diluted). Only claude-3-haiku pairs show extreme ratios (212×) due to near-zero ρ with nonlinear dependence.\n90\t**Disposition**: Remove as independent contribution. Optionally note in analysis: \"Gaussian copula fit is adequate for diverse model pools but breaks down for capability-mismatched pairs with nonlinear dependence.\"\n91\t**Strength**: DEAD as independent claim. May retain as minor observation.\n92\t\n93\t### Claim 6 (Practical): Robustness-First Panel Design\n94\t**Statement**: Optimal panel selection is robustness-first: (1) screen for individual robustness (η ≤ threshold), then (2) maximize K_eff among qualifying judges. The two-stage approach is critical because K_eff is harmful in unrestricted pools but may be neutral or beneficial among robustness-screened judges.\n95\t**Evidence** (15-model, 455 panels — fully validated):\n96\t- min(η_max) strategy dominates **12/12 conditions** (up from 5/6 at 6-model)\n97\t- ASR advantage range: +0.038 (arc×sycophancy) to +0.511 (arc×prompt_injection)\n98\t- Robust across panel sizes K=10, 20, 50\n99\t- Even in the sole K_eff-dominant condition (arc×position_bias), min_eta_max still outperforms max_K_eff\n100\t- Consistent with canonical regression: η_max 11/12 dominant\n101\t**Strength**: Strong (15-model fully confirmed). Zero failure conditions.\n102\t\n103\t### Claim 7 (Empirical+Practical): Aggregation Rule Modulates Both Vulnerability Drivers\n104\t**Statement**: Bayesian calibration partially mitigates BOTH vulnerability drivers — weakening η_max dominance AND reversing K_eff from harmful to protective. Different aggregation rules create a gradient from full dual-driver vulnerability (threshold) to partial mitigation (Bayesian).\n105\t**Evidence** (15-model, 455 panels, log-log canonical spec — D017, Reviewer-verified from JSON):\n106\t- Majority: η_max **11/12**, K_eff **8/12** (7+/1−), R²=0.298 ← canonical baseline (matches dominance table ✓)\n107\t- Weighted: η_max **9/12**, K_eff **9/12** (9+/0−), R²=0.284 — reduces both drivers but K_eff stays all positive\n108\t- Threshold: η_max **12/12**, K_eff **11/12** (10+/1−), R²=**0.890** — near-perfect fit under unanimity\n109\t- Bayesian: η_max **9/12** (↓), K_eff **7/12** (1+/**6 negative**), R²=0.104\n110\t- Key findings:\n111\t  - Bayesian weakens η_max (11→9/12) AND flips K_eff direction (majority 7+/1− → bayesian 1+/6−)\n112\t  - Threshold amplifies both channels: η_max 12/12, K_eff 11/12, R²=0.89 (unanimity maximizes dual-driver predictability)\n113\t  - Weighted reduces η_max (11→9/12) but K_eff stays all positive — accuracy weighting alone cannot reverse diversity harm\n114\t  - Only Bayesian calibration reverses K_eff direction (6/7 significant coefficients negative)\n115\t  - Aggregation gradient: threshold (max vulnerability) → majority → weighted → bayesian (min vulnerability)\n116\t**Strength**: Strong (log-log canonical, Reviewer-verified, sanity-checked against Claim 1). Prescriptive: robustness-first selection (Claim 6) + Bayesian aggregation = dual-channel defense stack.\n117\t\n118\t## Contribution Stack (ordered by strength, post-D019 reframe)\n119\t1. **Weakest-link dominance** — primary empirical (η_max robust 7-8/12 after all corrections; the strongest, most defensible finding)\n120\t2. **Aggregation as control lever** — empirical+practical (D017: Bayesian reverses K_eff direction, weakens η_max; threshold amplifies both; R²=0.89. Independent of non-independence concern)\n121\t3. **Attack-type taxonomy / GAM 6:6 split** — mechanistic (targeted=K_eff positive, shared-bias=K_eff negative; clean qualitative pattern; pending correct-tier validation)\n122\t4. **Robustness-first panel design** — practical (Claim 6: min_eta_max 12/12 wins; unaffected by SE correction)\n123\t5. **Methodological transparency on non-independence** — meta-contribution (demonstrating how OLS → clustered SE → mixed effects changes significance in combinatorial panel designs; useful for future work)\n124\t6. **Diversity-capability tradeoff** — empirical (r=0.70; structural, not affected by SE correction)\n125\t7. **Family label unreliability** — methodological (confirmed at 15-model scale)\n126\t7. **Adaptive vs random-fault predictability gap** — empirical (R² gap)\n127\t~~8. **Gaussian copula failure**~~ — REMOVED (falsified at 15-model scale; downgraded to minor observation)\n128\t\n129\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n130\t\n131\t### RC1: \"K_eff positive is just confound with η_max\"\n132\t**Response**: (a) Under standard OLS, K_eff is significant 8/12 (7+/1−), but after clustered SE correction K_eff drops to 0/12, mixed effects gives 3/12 — K_eff's independent effect is directionally positive but **statistically fragile**; (b) η_max remains robust at 7-8/12 under all corrections, confirming it is NOT a confound artifact; (c) GAM analysis reveals the K_eff direction cleanly splits by attack type (6:6 targeted vs shared-bias), suggesting real structure even if individual significance is fragile under correction; (d) We transparently report all three correction methods, which is itself a methodological contribution for combinatorial panel designs.\n133\t\n134\t### RC2: \"Why does diversity hurt? What's the mechanism?\"\n135\t**Response**: (a) BFT assumes random faults — independent nodes protect via uncorrelated failures; (b) Under adaptive adversaries, independent judges create diverse attack surface — attacker exploits judge-specific vulnerabilities; (c) GAM reveals the mechanism boundary: K_eff partial effect is positive for targeted attacks (6/6 conditions) and negative for shared-bias attacks (6/6 conditions). This clean split explains WHEN diversity helps vs hurts; (d) Note: K_eff's harmful direction is directional under OLS (7+/1−) but significance collapses under non-independence correction (0-3/12). The mechanism is real (GAM pattern), but its statistical strength is sensitive to correction — we report this transparently.\n136\t\n137\t### RC3: \"Only 15 models — does this generalize?\"\n138\t**Response**: (a) 15 models across 6 families, 3 capability tiers, covering major commercial and open-source models; (b) 455 panels provide strong statistical power; (c) Effect is robust to sensitivity analysis; (d) Direction consistent across 6→9→15 model scaling (K_eff shifts from NS to positive as model pool diversifies).\n139\t\n140\t### RC4: \"BFT comparison is a strawman\"\n141\t**Response**: (a) The implicit assumption \"more diverse judges = more robust\" is pervasive in LLM evaluation literature; (b) We formalize this assumption and show its reversal; (c) The BFT reversal mechanism (random vs adaptive faults) provides theoretical grounding beyond just empirical observation.\n142\t\n143\t### RC5: \"Why not just use the strongest models?\"\n144\t**Response**: (a) \"Strongest\" varies by attack type; (b) K_eff is the sole significant predictor in 1 condition (arc×position_bias) — even all-strong panels can be vulnerable through diversity channel; (c) Two-stage algorithm addresses both vulnerability drivers.\n145\t\n146\t### RC6: \"No theoretical novelty\"\n147\t**Response**: (a) Theorem 1 (η_max monotonicity) is formally proved; (b) BFT reversal mechanism provides novel theoretical framework; (c) Dual vulnerability driver finding with condition-dependent importance is new.\n148\t\n149\t### RC7: \"Why not just use Bayesian aggregation?\"\n150\t**Response**: (a) 15-model log-log canonical (D017, Reviewer-verified): Bayesian partially mitigates BOTH drivers — η_max drops to 9/12 (from 11/12), K_eff flips to 6/7 negative (protective). But it doesn't eliminate vulnerability: 9/12 η_max still significant, R² drops to 0.104 (residual vulnerability less predictable); (b) Requires clean accuracy prior which adaptive attackers could target; (c) Even under Bayesian, 9/12 conditions still show η_max vulnerability → robustness-first selection remains necessary; (d) Optimal defense stack: robustness-first selection (eliminates η_max) + Bayesian aggregation (flips K_eff to protective) = dual-channel coverage.\n151\t\n152\t### RC8: \"6-model and 15-model results contradict — which is right?\"\n153\t**Response**: (a) 6-model result (K_eff NS) was underpowered and confounded (r=-0.8, only 20 panels); (b) 15-model result (K_eff predominantly positive) has 23× more panels, wider capability range, and passes dominance analysis validation; (c) Paper reports both and explains why 15-model result is definitive; (d) The scaling behavior itself (K_eff effect emerging with more models) is informative.\n154\t\n155\t### RC9 (new): \"arc×sycophancy exception undermines your claim\"\n156\t**Response**: (a) Post-D019: arc×sycophancy K_eff is NOT significant after correction (OLS p=0.013 → clustered SE p=0.441 → mixed effects p=0.136). It is a directional observation, not a robust standalone finding; (b) However, GAM reveals that ALL shared-bias attacks (sycophancy, verbosity_bias, authority_bias × 2 benchmarks = 6 conditions) show negative K_eff partial effects, while ALL targeted attacks (6 conditions) show positive — the 6:6 split is the robust pattern, not the individual significance of arc×sycophancy; (c) This gives practitioners an actionable taxonomy: targeted attacks → diversity hurts, shared-bias attacks → diversity may help; (d) The structural pattern (GAM) is more informative than individual p-values under various corrections.\n157\t\n158\t## \"When Diversity Helps\" Section\n159\tDiversity IS beneficial under specific conditions — paper must present this as empirically grounded nuance, not just a hypothetical:\n160\t1. **Non-adversarial settings**: reducing calibration errors, position bias, verbosity bias in absence of adversary\n161\t2. **Shared-bias attacks (GAM-confirmed pattern)**: GAM reveals K_eff partial effect is negative (protective) for all 6 shared-bias conditions (sycophancy, verbosity_bias, authority_bias × 2 benchmarks). Note: arc×sycophancy K_eff was significant under standard OLS (p=0.013) but **not significant after clustered SE (p=0.441) or mixed effects (p=0.136)**. The directional pattern across all shared-bias attacks is the stronger evidence — individual significance is fragile under correction.\n162\t3. **After robustness screening**: once all judges exceed a capability threshold, K_eff's harmful effect may diminish (the diversity-capability tradeoff is broken by screening). This is the basis for our two-stage recommendation.\n163\t4. **Summary (post-D019)**: Under standard OLS, K_eff is positive in 7/12, NS in 4/12, negative in 1/12. Under clustered SE / mixed effects, K_eff significance collapses to 0-3/12. GAM reveals the underlying structure: targeted attacks → K_eff positive (6/6), shared-bias → K_eff negative (6/6). The attack-type taxonomy is the robust finding; individual K_eff significance counts are sensitive to SE correction.\n164\t\n165\t## Story Arc (v5: Post-D019 Reframe)\n166\t1. **Background**: Multi-judge LLM evaluation is increasingly adopted; diversity is assumed to be the key defense against manipulation (BFT analogy)\n167\t2. **Tension**: We test this assumption at unprecedented scale — 15 models, 6 families, 455 panels, 6 attack types\n168\t3. **Surprise**: Panel vulnerability is **robustly dominated by the weakest individual judge** (η_max 7-8/12 after clustered SE / mixed-effects correction). Diversity (K_eff) shows directional but statistically fragile association — significance collapses from 8/12 (OLS) to 0-3/12 after correcting for non-independence of panel observations\n169\t4. **Mechanistic nuance**: GAM analysis reveals K_eff's direction cleanly splits by attack type: positive (harmful) for targeted attacks, negative (protective) for shared-bias attacks — a 6:6 pattern masked by linear regression\n170\t5. **Aggregation as control lever**: Voting rule choice fundamentally modulates vulnerability — Bayesian calibration reverses K_eff direction (6/7 negative) and weakens η_max (9/12), while threshold voting amplifies both (R²=0.89)\n171\t6. **Defense**: Robustness-first screening (min η_max, 12/12 wins) + Bayesian aggregation = dual-channel defense stack\n172\t7. **Implication**: Panel security is primarily an individual-judge quality problem, not a diversity problem. But aggregation design and attack-type awareness provide complementary defense levers\n173\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca7c92ca-7226-4597-b435-bb7be4a94344","uuid":"8bdd24a0-f70d-48bf-bbb8-2ea6c7b87d99","timestamp":"2026-05-22T22:36:25.784Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/cert_manip_resist_eval/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T221131/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — cert_manip_resist_eval (v5: Post-Clustered-SE Reframe, D019)\n\n> Last updated: 2026-05-22 | Reason: Bootstrap v2 (Reviewer-verified): η_max 5-11/12 (bootstrap 5/12 most reliable), K_eff 0-1/12. η_max:K_eff ratio 5:1 confirms dominance. GAM 6:6 split confirmed. Aggregation gradient independent.\n\n## Target\nEMNLP 2026 (via ARR)\n\n## Title Candidates\n1. \"The Weakest Judge Wins: What Really Drives LLM Evaluation Panel Vulnerability Under Adversarial Attack\"\n2. \"Weakest Link, Not Diversity: Adversarial Vulnerability in Multi-Judge LLM Evaluation\"\n3. \"The Diversity Trap: Why Adding More Judges Doesn't Make LLM Evaluation Safer\" (softened with honest reporting)\n\n## Core Insight\nMulti-judge LLM evaluation panels are widely assumed to benefit from judge diversity. We conduct the first large-scale empirical study (15 models, 455 panels, 6 attacks, 2 benchmarks) decomposing panel vulnerability into individual weakness (η_max) and structural diversity (K_eff). Key findings: (1) **η_max dominates** panel vulnerability (5-11/12 conditions significant depending on correction method; wild cluster bootstrap — the most reliable method for small cluster counts — gives 5/12, with η_max:K_eff ratio of 5:1); (2) K_eff shows **directional but statistically fragile** association with vulnerability — point estimates predominantly positive (diversity increases risk), but significance collapses from 8/12 (OLS) to 0-1/12 after non-independence correction (bootstrap 1/12, clustered SE 0/12); (3) **GAM reveals a clean attack-type split**: K_eff is positive (harmful) for targeted attacks and negative (protective) for shared-bias attacks — a 6:6 pattern masked by linear regression; (4) **Aggregation rule choice fundamentally modulates vulnerability**: Bayesian calibration reverses K_eff direction (6/7 negative) and weakens η_max (9/12), while threshold voting amplifies both (R²=0.89).\n\n## Hook\n\"Panel security against adversarial manipulation is dominated by the weakest individual judge — not panel diversity. But how you aggregate judges' votes determines whether diversity becomes a vulnerability or a defense.\"\n\n## Novelty Positioning\nWe do NOT claim diversity is harmful with high statistical confidence — K_eff's independent effect is directional but fragile under rigorous correction. Our contributions are:\n1. **First large-scale empirical decomposition** of panel vulnerability into η_max and K_eff in the LLM-judge domain (15 models, 455 panels), with transparent robustness analysis showing η_max dominates (5:1 over K_eff under bootstrap inference)\n2. **Attack-type taxonomy with clean mechanistic split**: GAM reveals K_eff positive for targeted attacks, negative for shared-bias attacks (6:6 split), explaining WHEN diversity helps vs hurts\n3. **Aggregation as a control lever**: voting rule modulates the diversity-vulnerability relationship — Bayesian reverses K_eff direction, threshold amplifies it (D017, independent of non-independence concern)\n4. **Robustness-first panel design**: min(η_max) strategy wins 12/12 conditions (Claim 6, unaffected by SE correction)\n5. **Structural barriers**: diversity-capability tradeoff (r=0.70), family label unreliability (confirmed at 15-model)\n6. **Alternative diversity metrics robustness**: η_max dominance holds across operationalizations — Q-stat only 2/12 sig (r=0.674 with K_eff), disagreement 8/12, κ-diversity 7/12. K_eff practical effect size: IQR → Δ ASR = 1.3pp (directional but practically small)\n7. **Methodological transparency**: explicit reporting of how significance changes across OLS → clustered SE → mixed effects, demonstrating the importance of accounting for panel overlap in combinatorial evaluation designs\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (Primary): Weakest-Link Dominance\n**Statement**: Under adaptive adversarial attacks, panel vulnerability is **dominated by individual judge weakness (η_max)**. η_max remains significant in 5-8/12 conditions after non-independence correction (wild bootstrap 5/12, clustered SE 8/12, mixed effects 7/12). K_eff (diversity) shows directional association but significance is fragile (bootstrap 1/12, clustered SE 0/12). The η_max:K_eff dominance ratio is 5:1 under bootstrap — stronger than OLS's 11:8 ≈ 1.4:1.\n**Evidence** (15-model, 455 panels, 12 conditions, D019+D021):\n- **Regression spec**: log-log OLS: log(ASR + ε) ~ const + log(K_eff) + log(η_max + ε)\n- **Standard OLS**: η_max **11/12**, K_eff **8/12** (7+/1−) — inflated by panel non-independence\n- **Wild cluster bootstrap v2** (Reviewer-verified, B=9999, Rademacher, 3-position max-p): η_max **5/12**, K_eff **1/12** (mmlu×PI only) — conservative lower bound. Per-position analysis: position 0 gives 6/12 (cluster imbalance: claude-3-haiku=91 panels vs qwen2.5-14b=1), positions 1&2 each give **9/12** (more balanced clusters, consistent with clustered SE). Max-across-positions is legitimate conservative bound but tightened by position 0 imbalance.\n- **Clustered SE** (15 judge clusters, CR1): η_max **8/12**, K_eff **0/12** — consistent with per-position bootstrap 1&2\n- **Mixed effects** (random judge intercepts): η_max **7/12**, K_eff **3/12** (mmlu×PI, arc×PI, arc×PB)\n- SE inflation ~2.5x (consistent with 91/455 panel overlap)\n- Bootstrap η_max shows benchmark asymmetry: MMLU 4/6, ARC 1/6 survive. Likely cause: MMLU 4-choice format provides more scoring variance than ARC 2-choice, giving η_max more signal. arc×PI η_max completely lost (OLS p=3e-14 → bootstrap all NS) — signal was entirely from panel overlap.\n- **arc×sycophancy exception**: No longer significant under any correction (OLS p=0.013 → bootstrap 0.06 → clustered 0.441 → mixed 0.136). Reported as directional observation, not robust claim.\n- **Alternative diversity metrics (OLS)**: Q-stat 2/12, disagreement 8/12 (7+/1−), κ-diversity 7/12 (7+/0−). Q-stat (lowest correlation with K_eff, r=0.674) gives lowest diversity significance — further supports η_max as dominant driver regardless of diversity operationalization.\n- **Practical effect size**: K_eff IQR change → Δ ASR = 1.3pp (clustered SE CIs contain zero in 11/12 conditions). Even under OLS, diversity effect is practically small.\n**Strength**: η_max dominant (5:1 ratio over K_eff under bootstrap). Absolute significance lower than OLS (5/12 vs 11/12) but relative dominance stronger. K_eff directional but fragile and practically small.\n**Headline**: \"η_max dominates panel vulnerability (5:1 over K_eff); both channels inflated by panel non-independence, but η_max survives correction while K_eff does not.\"\n\n### Claim 1b (Secondary): Attack-Type Taxonomy — GAM 6:6 Split\n**Statement**: GAM analysis reveals that K_eff's direction cleanly splits by attack mechanism: **positive (diversity harmful) for targeted attacks** (prompt_injection, score_manipulation, position_bias × 2 benchmarks = 6 conditions) and **negative (diversity protective) for shared-bias attacks** (sycophancy, verbosity_bias, authority_bias × 2 benchmarks = 6 conditions). This 6:6 pattern is masked by linear OLS which shows 7+/1−/4NS.\n**Evidence**: GAM partial effects, 455 panels, 12 conditions.\n- Targeted attacks (exploit judge-specific weaknesses): K_eff partial effect positive in all 6 conditions\n- Shared-bias attacks (exploit common cognitive biases): K_eff partial effect negative in all 6 conditions\n- **Caveat**: GAM significance of individual conditions needs clustered SE / bootstrapped CI (pending); the structural pattern is the main finding, not individual p-values\n**Strength**: Moderate-to-strong as qualitative taxonomic contribution. The clean 6:6 split provides mechanistic explanatory power beyond individual significance counts. Confirmed under correct 3/3/9 tier classification (GAM tier-fix rerun: all macro conclusions unchanged).\n\n### Claim 2 (Empirical): Predictability Gap — Panel Composition Explains RF But Not Adaptive Vulnerability\n**Statement**: Panel composition (η_max + K_eff) explains substantially more variance under random faults (R²=0.73-0.81) than under adaptive attacks (lower R²). K_eff is positively associated with vulnerability in BOTH regimes, but: under RF, this association is genuine (survives all corrections, 2/2); under adaptive, it is largely artifactual (0-1/12 after correction). Adaptive adversaries introduce strategic variance beyond what panel structure can predict.\n**Evidence** (15-model, 455 panels, D021+RF validation, Reviewer-verified):\n- **Random-fault regime** (error = 1 - clean_accuracy, Monte Carlo 10000):\n  - K_eff **positive** std_β = +0.215 (MMLU), +0.379 (ARC) — diversity associated with HIGHER error\n  - K_eff significant **2/2** under ALL correction methods (OLS, clustered SE, bootstrap)\n  - R² = 0.73-0.81 (highly predictable)\n- **Adaptive regime** (D021):\n  - K_eff also positive under OLS (7+/1−) but significance collapses to **0-1/12** after correction\n  - R² substantially lower\n- **Contrast**: NOT \"diversity helps under RF but hurts under adaptive\" — diversity is harmful in both. The contrast is: K_eff's harmful association is GENUINE under RF but INFLATED/ARTIFACTUAL under adaptive due to panel non-independence\n- ΔR² gap: RF regime is highly predictable from panel composition; adaptive regime is not\n**Correct interpretation**: Random faults are structurally determined by panel composition (hence high R² and genuine K_eff effect). Adaptive adversaries exploit weaknesses strategically, introducing variance that panel-level predictors cannot capture. K_eff in the adaptive regime appears significant under OLS only because of panel overlap inflation.\n**Strength**: Strong as predictability gap (R² contrast). The finding that K_eff is genuine under RF but artifactual under adaptive is a clean methodological insight about when non-independence correction matters most.\n\n### Claim 3 (Empirical): Diversity-Capability Tradeoff\n**Statement**: In the current LLM ecosystem, maximizing panel diversity (K_eff) structurally introduces less capable/robust models. The correlation r=+0.700 is a structural constraint — diversity and capability are partially opposed in the current model ecosystem.\n**Evidence**:\n- K_eff-η_max correlation: r = +0.700 (15-model)\n- Under standard OLS: K_eff significant 8/12 (7+/1−) after residualizing η_max\n- **D019 caveat**: Under clustered SE, K_eff drops to 0/12; mixed effects gives 3/12. The \"independent predictive effect\" of K_eff beyond η_max is directional but NOT statistically robust after correcting for non-independence. The structural correlation (r=0.700) itself is unaffected by SE correction — only the regression significance of K_eff as independent predictor changes.\n**Framing**: The tradeoff is real as a structural constraint (r=0.700). Whether K_eff has an independent causal effect beyond η_max cannot be confidently established from this data — K_eff's significance is fragile under correction, and the high confound makes disentanglement unreliable.\n**Strength**: Moderate (structural correlation strong; independent effect fragile). Causal language avoided.\n\n### Claim 4 (Methodological): Family Labels ≠ Diversity\n**Statement**: Model family labels (Qwen/Llama/Mistral/Anthropic/OpenAI/Google) do not predict judge independence. Capability proximity is the primary driver of inter-judge correlation.\n**Evidence**:\n- 6-model: Mann-Whitney U p=0.206, permutation p=0.427\n- **15-model (confirmed)**: p=0.179 (MMLU), p=0.385 (ARC). 14 within-family pairs, 91 cross-family pairs. Still not significant.\n- Within-family MI variance is high (e.g., llama-70b↔8b MI only 0.05 due to capability gap > family similarity)\n**Strength**: Moderate. Consistent across 6→15 model scaling.\n\n### ~~Claim 5 (Methodological): Gaussian Copula Failure~~ → DOWNGRADED to observation\n**Original statement**: Gaussian copula systematically underestimates MI by 10-21×.\n**15-model result**: MI_obs/MI_gaussian mean ratio = **0.93** (MMLU), **0.90** (ARC, robust). Copula fits well at 15-model scale. The 6-model 10-21× was a small-sample artifact (15 pairs → 105 pairs, extreme values diluted). Only claude-3-haiku pairs show extreme ratios (212×) due to near-zero ρ with nonlinear dependence.\n**Disposition**: Remove as independent contribution. Optionally note in analysis: \"Gaussian copula fit is adequate for diverse model pools but breaks down for capability-mismatched pairs with nonlinear dependence.\"\n**Strength**: DEAD as independent claim. May retain as minor observation.\n\n### Claim 6 (Practical): Robustness-First Panel Design\n**Statement**: Optimal panel selection is robustness-first: (1) screen for individual robustness (η ≤ threshold), then (2) maximize K_eff among qualifying judges. The two-stage approach is critical because K_eff is harmful in unrestricted pools but may be neutral or beneficial among robustness-screened judges.\n**Evidence** (15-model, 455 panels — fully validated):\n- min(η_max) strategy dominates **12/12 conditions** (up from 5/6 at 6-model)\n- ASR advantage range: +0.038 (arc×sycophancy) to +0.511 (arc×prompt_injection)\n- Robust across panel sizes K=10, 20, 50\n- Even in the sole K_eff-dominant condition (arc×position_bias), min_eta_max still outperforms max_K_eff\n- Consistent with canonical regression: η_max 11/12 dominant\n**Strength**: Strong (15-model fully confirmed). Zero failure conditions.\n\n### Claim 7 (Empirical+Practical): Aggregation Rule Modulates Both Vulnerability Drivers\n**Statement**: Bayesian calibration partially mitigates BOTH vulnerability drivers — weakening η_max dominance AND reversing K_eff from harmful to protective. Different aggregation rules create a gradient from full dual-driver vulnerability (threshold) to partial mitigation (Bayesian).\n**Evidence** (15-model, 455 panels, log-log canonical spec — D017, Reviewer-verified from JSON):\n- Majority: η_max **11/12**, K_eff **8/12** (7+/1−), R²=0.298 ← canonical baseline (matches dominance table ✓)\n- Weighted: η_max **9/12**, K_eff **9/12** (9+/0−), R²=0.284 — reduces both drivers but K_eff stays all positive\n- Threshold: η_max **12/12**, K_eff **11/12** (10+/1−), R²=**0.890** — near-perfect fit under unanimity\n- Bayesian: η_max **9/12** (↓), K_eff **7/12** (1+/**6 negative**), R²=0.104\n- Key findings:\n  - Bayesian weakens η_max (11→9/12) AND flips K_eff direction (majority 7+/1− → bayesian 1+/6−)\n  - Threshold amplifies both channels: η_max 12/12, K_eff 11/12, R²=0.89 (unanimity maximizes dual-driver predictability)\n  - Weighted reduces η_max (11→9/12) but K_eff stays all positive — accuracy weighting alone cannot reverse diversity harm\n  - Only Bayesian calibration reverses K_eff direction (6/7 significant coefficients negative)\n  - Aggregation gradient: threshold (max vulnerability) → majority → weighted → bayesian (min vulnerability)\n**Strength**: Strong (log-log canonical, Reviewer-verified, sanity-checked against Claim 1). Prescriptive: robustness-first selection (Claim 6) + Bayesian aggregation = dual-channel defense stack.\n\n## Contribution Stack (ordered by strength, post-D019 reframe)\n1. **Weakest-link dominance** — primary empirical (η_max robust 7-8/12 after all corrections; the strongest, most defensible finding)\n2. **Aggregation as control lever** — empirical+practical (D017: Bayesian reverses K_eff direction, weakens η_max; threshold amplifies both; R²=0.89. Independent of non-independence concern)\n3. **Attack-type taxonomy / GAM 6:6 split** — mechanistic (targeted=K_eff positive, shared-bias=K_eff negative; clean qualitative pattern; pending correct-tier validation)\n4. **Robustness-first panel design** — practical (Claim 6: min_eta_max 12/12 wins; unaffected by SE correction)\n5. **Methodological transparency on non-independence** — meta-contribution (demonstrating how OLS → clustered SE → mixed effects changes significance in combinatorial panel designs; useful for future work)\n6. **Diversity-capability tradeoff** — empirical (r=0.70; structural, not affected by SE correction)\n7. **Family label unreliability** — methodological (confirmed at 15-model scale)\n7. **Adaptive vs random-fault predictability gap** — empirical (R² gap)\n~~8. **Gaussian copula failure**~~ — REMOVED (falsified at 15-model scale; downgraded to minor observation)\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### RC1: \"K_eff positive is just confound with η_max\"\n**Response**: (a) Under standard OLS, K_eff is significant 8/12 (7+/1−), but after clustered SE correction K_eff drops to 0/12, mixed effects gives 3/12 — K_eff's independent effect is directionally positive but **statistically fragile**; (b) η_max remains robust at 7-8/12 under all corrections, confirming it is NOT a confound artifact; (c) GAM analysis reveals the K_eff direction cleanly splits by attack type (6:6 targeted vs shared-bias), suggesting real structure even if individual significance is fragile under correction; (d) We transparently report all three correction methods, which is itself a methodological contribution for combinatorial panel designs.\n\n### RC2: \"Why does diversity hurt? What's the mechanism?\"\n**Response**: (a) BFT assumes random faults — independent nodes protect via uncorrelated failures; (b) Under adaptive adversaries, independent judges create diverse attack surface — attacker exploits judge-specific vulnerabilities; (c) GAM reveals the mechanism boundary: K_eff partial effect is positive for targeted attacks (6/6 conditions) and negative for shared-bias attacks (6/6 conditions). This clean split explains WHEN diversity helps vs hurts; (d) Note: K_eff's harmful direction is directional under OLS (7+/1−) but significance collapses under non-independence correction (0-3/12). The mechanism is real (GAM pattern), but its statistical strength is sensitive to correction — we report this transparently.\n\n### RC3: \"Only 15 models — does this generalize?\"\n**Response**: (a) 15 models across 6 families, 3 capability tiers, covering major commercial and open-source models; (b) 455 panels provide strong statistical power; (c) Effect is robust to sensitivity analysis; (d) Direction consistent across 6→9→15 model scaling (K_eff shifts from NS to positive as model pool diversifies).\n\n### RC4: \"BFT comparison is a strawman\"\n**Response**: (a) The implicit assumption \"more diverse judges = more robust\" is pervasive in LLM evaluation literature; (b) We formalize this assumption and show its reversal; (c) The BFT reversal mechanism (random vs adaptive faults) provides theoretical grounding beyond just empirical observation.\n\n### RC5: \"Why not just use the strongest models?\"\n**Response**: (a) \"Strongest\" varies by attack type; (b) K_eff is the sole significant predictor in 1 condition (arc×position_bias) — even all-strong panels can be vulnerable through diversity channel; (c) Two-stage algorithm addresses both vulnerability drivers.\n\n### RC6: \"No theoretical novelty\"\n**Response**: (a) Theorem 1 (η_max monotonicity) is formally proved; (b) BFT reversal mechanism provides novel theoretical framework; (c) Dual vulnerability driver finding with condition-dependent importance is new.\n\n### RC7: \"Why not just use Bayesian aggregation?\"\n**Response**: (a) 15-model log-log canonical (D017, Reviewer-verified): Bayesian partially mitigates BOTH drivers — η_max drops to 9/12 (from 11/12), K_eff flips to 6/7 negative (protective). But it doesn't eliminate vulnerability: 9/12 η_max still significant, R² drops to 0.104 (residual vulnerability less predictable); (b) Requires clean accuracy prior which adaptive attackers could target; (c) Even under Bayesian, 9/12 conditions still show η_max vulnerability → robustness-first selection remains necessary; (d) Optimal defense stack: robustness-first selection (eliminates η_max) + Bayesian aggregation (flips K_eff to protective) = dual-channel coverage.\n\n### RC8: \"6-model and 15-model results contradict — which is right?\"\n**Response**: (a) 6-model result (K_eff NS) was underpowered and confounded (r=-0.8, only 20 panels); (b) 15-model result (K_eff predominantly positive) has 23× more panels, wider capability range, and passes dominance analysis validation; (c) Paper reports both and explains why 15-model result is definitive; (d) The scaling behavior itself (K_eff effect emerging with more models) is informative.\n\n### RC9 (new): \"arc×sycophancy exception undermines your claim\"\n**Response**: (a) Post-D019: arc×sycophancy K_eff is NOT significant after correction (OLS p=0.013 → clustered SE p=0.441 → mixed effects p=0.136). It is a directional observation, not a robust standalone finding; (b) However, GAM reveals that ALL shared-bias attacks (sycophancy, verbosity_bias, authority_bias × 2 benchmarks = 6 conditions) show negative K_eff partial effects, while ALL targeted attacks (6 conditions) show positive — the 6:6 split is the robust pattern, not the individual significance of arc×sycophancy; (c) This gives practitioners an actionable taxonomy: targeted attacks → diversity hurts, shared-bias attacks → diversity may help; (d) The structural pattern (GAM) is more informative than individual p-values under various corrections.\n\n## \"When Diversity Helps\" Section\nDiversity IS beneficial under specific conditions — paper must present this as empirically grounded nuance, not just a hypothetical:\n1. **Non-adversarial settings**: reducing calibration errors, position bias, verbosity bias in absence of adversary\n2. **Shared-bias attacks (GAM-confirmed pattern)**: GAM reveals K_eff partial effect is negative (protective) for all 6 shared-bias conditions (sycophancy, verbosity_bias, authority_bias × 2 benchmarks). Note: arc×sycophancy K_eff was significant under standard OLS (p=0.013) but **not significant after clustered SE (p=0.441) or mixed effects (p=0.136)**. The directional pattern across all shared-bias attacks is the stronger evidence — individual significance is fragile under correction.\n3. **After robustness screening**: once all judges exceed a capability threshold, K_eff's harmful effect may diminish (the diversity-capability tradeoff is broken by screening). This is the basis for our two-stage recommendation.\n4. **Summary (post-D019)**: Under standard OLS, K_eff is positive in 7/12, NS in 4/12, negative in 1/12. Under clustered SE / mixed effects, K_eff significance collapses to 0-3/12. GAM reveals the underlying structure: targeted attacks → K_eff positive (6/6), shared-bias → K_eff negative (6/6). The attack-type taxonomy is the robust finding; individual K_eff significance counts are sensitive to SE correction.\n\n## Story Arc (v5: Post-D019 Reframe)\n1. **Background**: Multi-judge LLM evaluation is increasingly adopted; diversity is assumed to be the key defense against manipulation (BFT analogy)\n2. **Tension**: We test this assumption at unprecedented scale — 15 models, 6 families, 455 panels, 6 attack types\n3. **Surprise**: Panel vulnerability is **robustly dominated by the weakest individual judge** (η_max 7-8/12 after clustered SE / mixed-effects correction). Diversity (K_eff) shows directional but statistically fragile association — significance collapses from 8/12 (OLS) to 0-3/12 after correcting for non-independence of panel observations\n4. **Mechanistic nuance**: GAM analysis reveals K_eff's direction cleanly splits by attack type: positive (harmful) for targeted attacks, negative (protective) for shared-bias attacks — a 6:6 pattern masked by linear regression\n5. **Aggregation as control lever**: Voting rule choice fundamentally modulates vulnerability — Bayesian calibration reverses K_eff direction (6/7 negative) and weakens η_max (9/12), while threshold voting amplifies both (R²=0.89)\n6. **Defense**: Robustness-first screening (min η_max, 12/12 wins) + Bayesian aggregation = dual-channel defense stack\n7. **Implication**: Panel security is primarily an individual-judge quality problem, not a diversity problem. But aggregation design and attack-type awareness provide complementary defense levers\n","numLines":173,"startLine":1,"totalLines":173}}}
